{"event": "user", "message": {"content": "You are the existing independent reviewer in actual conversation fe7486d5-c674-4f04-9f52-ef41e1eff966, in its ORIGINAL fresh-provider cwd. You previously reviewed unchanged witness cache/stream and the saved-record projector, and the original five actual operations. You did not author this new consumer or its independent oracles. This is a NEW source/operation judgment on new bytes, not reuse of prior approval. Root is sole executor/integrator. All preparation is R-only. This request authorizes NO tools, filesystem reads, shell, model/owner/evaluator execution, code installation or W/Git action. All mandatory review bodies are inline. Externally pinned inventories/binaries/prior receipts are provenance and identity bindings, not a claim you freshly read their semantic bodies. Requested model is gemini-4-argon-high/HIGH pinned slug under existing Root selection; actual init identity/cwd/CID must remain recorded; no backend canonical-attestation claim.\n\nCandidate 33281 bytes SHA97975468466accb30fa5dc465bf58ecd48e95f41498bbfa0d611f98693bdca91 is an external explicit tests/support consumer only. No producer/library/owner/guard/budget/parser/admission source changes. It reuses the observed successful normal Core rlib SHA4afb66098943d7a3da24bcfd4e2930b30944f81d1b06268cf369ace9454fe873 and depinfo. No Core build or old passing three-case/cache/K/Quint/native prefix replay is selected. Exact proposed ordinary operations are one consumer compile30s and two NEW exact selectors10s each, with unchanged finite caps/full bounded streams; eligibility and source correctness require your fresh judgment. Both new tests are UNRUN. The source author knew one disclosed final work summary scalar214; it is not a literal/branch/assertion in Rust and full expected prefixes/schedule cells remained withheld. Do not describe that final scalar as fully blinded. Preserve this qualification, all raw B versus logical A distinctions, H1/unmeasured allocation/copy/drop/physical bytes-time, general hostile-WitnessPlan/omitted-dependency security obligations, no canonical ProjectRel/import/Link proof, semantic-refinement/native gaps and no whole035 acceptance.\n\nTwo manual parts form ONE opinion. This part's complete bodies are identified by ID, path, exact bytes and SHA. Read complete function/field bodies, not names or sampled ends. No final opinion before BOTH parts are complete in this same context. Do not invent APIs/paths/quotes/flags or infer PASS from a prepared assertion. If a body is incomplete/unreadable or you cannot assess a required field, state that precise gap; do not claim it read. Repeated object values in oracle delivery are losslessly factored, with all values, typed references, full expansion description and independently generated roundtrip proof supplied. That is full data delivery, not authority from a hash alone; inspect all factored values and mappings and relate them to the complete consumer comparisons.\n\nPART 1 OF 2: source, consumed APIs, requirements and exact commands. Read all 12 bodies below. Inspect actual source flow from fixed A source constructors through bounded copy/admit/admit_run/capture, SAME owner stream, cached and uncached saved observations, complete reference spans, complete A JSON equality, then actual B counters/rules/intervals. Validate the initial-only factorial3 seed performs zero owner steps; ordinary source mismatch checks only independently specified SourceAssociation category; first actual pending HelperEnter stops/resumes SAME image/cache without replay; exact error locator is UNBOUND. Verify Let/Unary/PatternVar source/wire declarations and all meaningful saved environments/frames/outcomes are consumed. Check the new factorial2 B schedule builds genesis+every actual B record and all interval joins directly from actual images/events before opaque expected JSON is parsed, including publication and charged bookkeeping. Never equate B counters to A charges. Full normative public rule-ID map is formatting data, not selected schedule membership. Review complete comparison/membership logic, three argv/env/cwd/output bindings and reused Core identity. Return only a concise PART1_READ_CHECKPOINT: list IDs and full-body coverage, concrete issues found, and FINAL_JUDGMENT_PENDING_PART2. Do not approve source/operations yet.\n\n\n=== BEGIN FULL BODY 01-full-clauses | /home/charl/Moriarty/.moriarty-dev/runtime/sherlock-review-20261017/witness-reference-contrast-review-20261018/bodies/01-ORIGINAL035-AND-SCON013-024.txt | 4608 bytes | SHA256 4ad84345278f7a0bff232bd6702fa5bbf5107ea02317f58dfc412f69e74b0f51 ===\nFull clause from openspec/changes/sherlock-universal-interpreter-design/specs/universal-interpreter/spec.md:253 (source SHA256 e593ecbe48e902ee430fa7c9d14a681100e27f71df297c5161c5881e3fb6311b)\n### Requirement: UIREQ-035 Deterministic witness dataflow\nWHEN a WitnessPlan is evaluated, its baseline SHALL execute a typed dependency DAG in a deterministic uncached order to materialize complete StepRecords.\n\n#### Scenario: Independent normal comparison baseline\n- **WHEN** The same admitted factorial/list/tree or pending-caller state is materialized without caching, with cold caches and with warm caches.\n- **THEN** Stable dependency ordering and explicit bindings produce identical decoded reference prefixes, ordered frames/environments, outcomes and reference-work observations against independently authored expectations. Cache/lifetime/streaming variants retain the uncached baseline; reusable keys include exact program/profile/layout and immutable inputs, while helper visits, copies, live values and memory remain separate diagnostics. Neither those expectations nor semantic behavior are generated from the materializer/DAG metadata.\n\n\nFull clause from openspec/changes/sherlock-completion-convergence/specs/sherlock-completion/spec.md:285 (source SHA256 67bc5e23fd4c3181f64c64941975258d0faf500e764859288cb7dfb19840836d)\n### Requirement: SCON-013 Deterministic witness baseline\n\nWHEN witness scheduling is evaluated, an uncached deterministic dependency baseline SHALL materialize all required records before cache/last-use/stream optimizations are compared, retaining logical occurrences and exact independent outputs.\n\nRetains: UIREQ-009, UIREQ-013, UIREQ-024, UIREQ-031, UIREQ-035; B-T06, B-T07, B-T14. Callable predicate: `witness_baseline_and_dependencies_complete`. Batch: B08.\n\nCurrent: UIREQ035/B-T07 baseline is v1, not a future optional experiment. Proposed acceptance remains OPEN.\n\n#### Scenario: SCON-013 positive observation\n\n- **WHEN** the independently frozen positive fixture is exercised through the named actual consumer\n- **THEN** Repeated shared leaves retain two occurrence charges; uncached and cached producers match every ordered field; helper visits, copies, live values and I/O are separately reported.\n\n#### Scenario: SCON-013 incomplete or contrasting observation\n\n- **WHEN** the corresponding incomplete, unsupported or boundary fixture is supplied or reached\n- **THEN** A cache hit cannot remove semantic work or pending frames; an omitted dependency yields incomplete output instead of fabricated default values; memory improvement is unclaimed without measured complete-path data.\n\n#### Final03 additive subclause: SCON-013.R02\n\nThe required uncached witness DAG SHALL identify definition, uses, lifetime unit and live-out representation for each boundary-required value. Required values survive or are reconstructed without changing complete decoded boundary state or residual duties. Storage reuse follows its existing owner-controlled mutability/storage contract; no foreign allocation policy or digest substitutes for required field comparison.\n\n\n\nFull clause from openspec/changes/sherlock-completion-convergence/specs/sherlock-completion/spec.md:553 (source SHA256 67bc5e23fd4c3181f64c64941975258d0faf500e764859288cb7dfb19840836d)\n### Requirement: SCON-024 Measured optimization claims\n\nWHEN an optimization is reported beneficial, the experiment SHALL bind matched complete workloads and sink behavior and measure declared preparation/build/execute/serialize/compare phases, total elapsed time and peak memory separately from reference work and target costs.\n\nRetains: UIREQ-013, UIREQ-024, UIREQ-025, UIREQ-031, UIREQ-032, UIREQ-033, UIREQ-035; B-T07, B-T08, B-T09, B-T14. Callable predicate: `matched_optimization_measurements_complete`. Batch: B08.\n\nCurrent: Measurements remain separately admitted; no performance gate/threshold is invented here. Proposed acceptance remains OPEN.\n\n#### Scenario: SCON-024 positive observation\n\n- **WHEN** the independently frozen positive fixture is exercised through the named actual consumer\n- **THEN** Compare deterministic baseline and candidate on the same complete workload and declared cache/reuse condition; callback-record-retaining QA sink is identified.\n\n#### Scenario: SCON-024 incomplete or contrasting observation\n\n- **WHEN** the corresponding incomplete, unsupported or boundary fixture is supplied or reached\n- **THEN** Unmeasured values stay absent with a reason; stream comparison does not imply reduced memory; logical lanes, sampled timings or reused receipts are not measured full-path native cost.\n\n\n=== END FULL BODY 01-full-clauses ===\n\n=== BEGIN FULL BODY 02-full-new-consumer | /home/charl/Moriarty/.moriarty-dev/runtime/sherlock-review-20261017/witness-reference-contrast-source-20261018/revision02-B0-schedule/afterimages/crates/mori-core/tests/support/sherlock_witness_reference_contrast_positive.rs | 33281 bytes | SHA256 97975468466accb30fa5dc465bf58ecd48e95f41498bbfa0d611f98693bdca91 ===\n//! Explicit normal consumer of actual saved owner records, not Cargo autodiscovery.\n//! Expected prefix bodies are independent opaque includes, never producer inputs.\n//! New countercases advance one real B image each; old passing prefixes are not replayed.\n//! Cache contrast seeds only a valid fact3 startup capture, with zero source steps.\nuse mori_core::sherlock as a;\nuse a::helper_machine::{complete_observation as co, reference_projection as rp, witness_plan as wp, source_input_bridge as bridge};\nuse a::helper_machine::shared::*;\nuse a::helper_machine::shared::owner_host::host_owner_engine;\nuse serde_json::{json, Value as J};\nuse std::sync::Arc;\n\n\nfn tree(t: &a::Tree) -> J { match t {\n    a::Tree::Leaf(n) => json!({\"Leaf\":n}),\n    a::Tree::Branch(l,r) => json!({\"Branch\":[tree(l),tree(r)]}),\n} }\nfn value(v: &a::Value) -> J { match v {\n    a::Value::UInt(n)=>json!({\"UInt\":n}),a::Value::Bool(b)=>json!({\"Bool\":b}),\n    a::Value::List(xs)=>json!({\"List\":xs}),a::Value::Tree(t)=>json!({\"Tree\":tree(t)}),\n} }\nfn env(e: &a::Environment) -> J { J::Array(e.iter().map(|(n,v)|json!({\"name\":n,\"value\":value(v)})).collect()) }\nfn pattern(p:&a::Pattern)->J { match p {\n    a::Pattern::Var(n)=>json!({\"Var\":n}),a::Pattern::Nil=>json!({\"Nil\":null}),\n    a::Pattern::Cons(x,y)=>json!({\"Cons\":[x,y]}),a::Pattern::Leaf(n)=>json!({\"Leaf\":n}),\n    a::Pattern::Branch(x,y)=>json!({\"Branch\":[x,y]}),\n} }\nfn arm(x:&a::Arm)->J {json!({\"pattern\":pattern(&x.pattern),\"body\":expr(&x.body)})}\nfn arms(xs:&[a::Arm])->J {J::Array(xs.iter().map(arm).collect())}\nfn expr(x:&a::Expr)->J {match x {\n    a::Expr::Literal(v)=>json!({\"Literal\":value(v)}),a::Expr::Var(n)=>json!({\"Var\":n}),\n    a::Expr::Let(n,x,y)=>json!({\"Let\":{\"name\":n,\"value\":expr(x),\"body\":expr(y)}}),\n    a::Expr::Binary(op,x,y)=>json!({\"Binary\":{\"op\":format!(\"{op:?}\"),\"left\":expr(x),\"right\":expr(y)}}),\n    a::Expr::Unary(op,x)=>json!({\"Unary\":{\"op\":format!(\"{op:?}\"),\"operand\":expr(x)}}),\n    a::Expr::If(x,y,z)=>json!({\"If\":{\"condition\":expr(x),\"yes\":expr(y),\"no\":expr(z)}}),\n    a::Expr::Call(n,xs)=>json!({\"Call\":{\"name\":n,\"args\":xs.iter().map(|x|expr(x)).collect::<Vec<_>>()}}),\n    a::Expr::Match(x,xs)=>json!({\"Match\":{\"value\":expr(x),\"arms\":arms(xs)}}),\n} }\nfn function(f:&a::Function)->J {json!({\"name\":f.name,\"parameters\":f.parameters.iter().map(|p|json!({\"name\":p.name,\"ty\":format!(\"{:?}\",p.ty)})).collect::<Vec<_>>(),\"return_type\":format!(\"{:?}\",f.return_type),\"body\":expr(&f.body)})}\nfn program(p:&a::Program)->J {json!({\"functions\":p.functions.iter().map(function).collect::<Vec<_>>(),\"entry\":expr(&p.entry)})}\nfn frame(f:&a::Frame)->J {match f {\n    a::Frame::Let(n,b,e)=>json!({\"Let\":{\"name\":n,\"body\":expr(b),\"saved_environment\":env(e)}}),\n    a::Frame::Left(op,r,e)=>json!({\"Left\":{\"op\":format!(\"{op:?}\"),\"right\":expr(r),\"saved_environment\":env(e)}}),\n    a::Frame::Right(op,l)=>json!({\"Right\":{\"op\":format!(\"{op:?}\"),\"left\":value(l)}}),\n    a::Frame::Unary(op)=>json!({\"Unary\":{\"op\":format!(\"{op:?}\")}}),\n    a::Frame::If(y,n,e)=>json!({\"If\":{\"yes\":expr(y),\"no\":expr(n),\"saved_environment\":env(e)}}),\n    a::Frame::Match(xs,e)=>json!({\"Match\":{\"arms\":arms(xs),\"saved_environment\":env(e)}}),\n    a::Frame::Args(n,vs,xs,e)=>json!({\"Args\":{\"function_name\":n,\"completed_values\":vs.iter().map(value).collect::<Vec<_>>(),\"remaining_exprs\":xs.iter().map(|x|expr(x)).collect::<Vec<_>>(),\"saved_environment\":env(e)}}),\n    a::Frame::Return(t,e)=>json!({\"Return\":{\"expected_type\":format!(\"{t:?}\"),\"saved_environment\":env(e)}}),\n    a::Frame::Scope(e)=>json!({\"Scope\":{\"saved_environment\":env(e)}}),\n} }\nfn control(c:&a::Control)->J {match c {\n    a::Control::Eval(x)=>json!({\"Eval\":expr(x)}),a::Control::Return(v)=>json!({\"Return\":value(v)}),\n    a::Control::Push(f,c,e)=>json!({\"Push\":{\"frame\":frame(f),\"next\":control(c),\"environment\":env(e)}}),\n    a::Control::Invoke(n,vs)=>json!({\"Invoke\":{\"name\":n,\"values\":vs.iter().map(value).collect::<Vec<_>>()}}),\n    a::Control::Enter(f,vs)=>json!({\"Enter\":{\"function\":f.as_ref().map(function),\"values\":vs.iter().map(value).collect::<Vec<_>>()}}),\n    a::Control::Bound(e,t,b)=>json!({\"Bound\":{\"bindings\":e.as_ref().map(env),\"type\":format!(\"{t:?}\"),\"body\":expr(b)}}),\n    a::Control::Cases(v,xs,e)=>json!({\"Cases\":{\"value\":value(v),\"arms\":arms(xs),\"saved_environment\":env(e)}}),\n    a::Control::CaseResult(b,v,x,xs,e)=>json!({\"CaseResult\":{\"bindings\":b.as_ref().map(env),\"value\":value(v),\"body\":expr(x),\"remaining_arms\":arms(xs),\"saved_environment\":env(e)}}),\n    a::Control::PrimitiveResult(Ok(v))=>json!({\"PrimitiveResult\":{\"Ok\":value(v)}}),\n    a::Control::PrimitiveResult(Err(c))=>json!({\"PrimitiveResult\":{\"Err\":c}}),\n    a::Control::Error(c)=>json!({\"Error\":c}),\n} }\nfn outcome(o:&a::Outcome)->J {match o {\n    a::Outcome::Pending=>json!(\"Pending\"),a::Outcome::Done(v)=>json!({\"Done\":value(v)}),\n    a::Outcome::Rejected(c)=>json!({\"Rejected\":c}),a::Outcome::Exhausted=>json!(\"Exhausted\"),\n} }\nfn snapshot(s:&a::Snapshot)->J {json!({\"program\":program(&s.program),\"control\":s.control.as_ref().map(control),\"environment\":env(&s.environment),\"frames_top_first\":s.frames.iter().map(frame).collect::<Vec<_>>(),\"stack_limit\":s.stack_limit,\"remaining_fuel\":s.remaining_fuel,\"initial_fuel\":s.initial_fuel,\"outcome\":outcome(&s.outcome)})}\n\nfn literal(v:a::Value)->a::ExprRef {Arc::new(a::Expr::Literal(v))}\nfn uint(n:u128)->a::ExprRef {literal(a::Value::UInt(n))}\nfn var(n:&str)->a::ExprRef {Arc::new(a::Expr::Var(n.into()))}\nfn binary(op:a::BinaryOp,x:a::ExprRef,y:a::ExprRef)->a::ExprRef {Arc::new(a::Expr::Binary(op,x,y))}\nfn call(n:&str,x:a::ExprRef)->a::ExprRef {Arc::new(a::Expr::Call(n.into(),vec![x]))}\nfn one_function(n:&str,p:&str,t:a::Type,b:a::ExprRef,arg:a::ExprRef)->Arc<a::Program> {Arc::new(a::Program{functions:vec![a::Function{name:n.into(),parameters:vec![a::Parameter{name:p.into(),ty:t}],return_type:a::Type::UInt,body:b}],entry:call(n,arg)})}\nfn factorial(entry_n:u128)->Arc<a::Program> {one_function(\"fact\",\"n\",a::Type::UInt,Arc::new(a::Expr::If(binary(a::BinaryOp::Eq,var(\"n\"),uint(0)),uint(1),binary(a::BinaryOp::Mul,var(\"n\"),call(\"fact\",binary(a::BinaryOp::Sub,var(\"n\"),uint(1)))))),uint(entry_n))}\n\nfn layout() -> (BoundsC, LayoutSchemaC) {\n    let bounds = BoundsC {\n        code_rows: 64, function_rows: 4, code_child_slots: 16, parameter_slots: 8,\n        pattern_rows: 8, match_plan_rows: 8, match_arm_rows: 8, type_rows: 8,\n        constructor_rows: 8, constructor_field_slots: 16, max_arity: 8,\n        constant_nodes: 16, constant_field_slots: 16, data_nodes: 64,\n        data_field_slots: 64, environment_cells: 64, frames: 64, helper_tasks: 64,\n        serialization_bytes: 65536, max_reference_work: 4096,\n        max_helper_work: 4096, step_cap: 4096,\n    };\n    let schema = LayoutSchemaC {\n        layout_version: (\"moriarty\".into(), \"sherlock-helper-microstep-hostonly/1\".into()),\n        field_id: None, widths: None, scalar_layout_id: None, bounds,\n        capacities: LayoutCapacitiesC {\n            name_rows: 32, name_bytes: 256, occurrence_path_slots: 256, value_slots: 4096,\n        }, boundary_capacities_present: false,\n    };\n    (bounds, schema)\n}\n\nfn tooling<T>(r:Result<T,Tooling>)->T {match r {\n    Ok(x)=>x,\n    Err(Tooling::AdmissionRejected{reason,detail,locator})=>panic!(\"admission {reason:?} {detail} {locator:?}\"),\n    Err(Tooling::CapacityNotAdmitted{kind,needed,limit,locator})=>panic!(\"capacity {kind:?} {needed:?}/{limit} {locator:?}\"),\n    Err(Tooling::UnsupportedFeature{feature,locator})=>panic!(\"feature {feature:?} {locator:?}\"),\n}}\n// Reconstruct the SAME saved observation. No owner/reference transition occurs.\nfn variants(s:&wp::StrategyMaterializedSnapshot)->Vec<wp::DecodedSnapshot> {\n    let baseline=wp::evaluate_uncached(&s.plan,&s.raw).expect(\"uncached actual witness\");\n    assert_eq!(s.evaluation.witness.decoded,baseline.decoded);\n    let last=wp::evaluate_last_use(&s.plan,&s.raw).expect(\"last-use actual witness\");\n    let mut cache=wp::WitnessCache::default();\n    let cold=wp::evaluate_memoized(&s.plan,&s.raw,&mut cache,wp::SlotStorage::RetainAll).expect(\"cold actual witness\");\n    let warm=wp::evaluate_memoized(&s.plan,&s.raw,&mut cache,wp::SlotStorage::LastUse).expect(\"warm actual witness\");\n    assert!(cold.scheduling.scope_reset); assert_eq!(cold.scheduling.cache_hits,0);\n    assert!(!warm.scheduling.scope_reset); assert_eq!(warm.scheduling.cache_misses,0);\n    assert_eq!(warm.scheduling.cache_hits,s.plan.nodes.len()-s.plan.inputs.len());\n    assert_eq!(warm.witness.diagnostics.input_reads,s.plan.inputs.len());\n    assert_eq!(warm.witness.diagnostics.value_constructions,0);\n    assert_eq!(warm.witness.diagnostics.environment_constructions,0);\n    assert_eq!(warm.witness.diagnostics.payload_constructions,0);\n    let live=s.plan.live_outs.iter().copied().collect::<std::collections::BTreeSet<_>>().len();\n    assert_eq!(last.scheduling.retained_slots_at_publication,live);\n    assert_eq!(last.scheduling.reclaimed_slots,s.plan.nodes.len()-live);\n    assert_eq!(warm.witness.diagnostics.measured_host_bytes,None);\n    assert_eq!(warm.witness.diagnostics.measured_host_time_ns,None);\n    let variants=vec![baseline.decoded,last.witness.decoded,cold.witness.decoded,warm.witness.decoded,s.evaluation.witness.decoded.clone()];\n    for decoded in &variants {assert_eq!(decoded,&variants[0]);}\n    variants\n}\nfn exercise(p:Arc<a::Program>,frozen:&str,ordinary_probes:bool) {\n    let budget=bridge::SourceCopyBudget{max_functions:4,max_parameters_per_function:8,max_total_parameters:8,max_expr_nodes:128,max_copy_depth:32,max_match_arms:16,max_name_bytes:512,max_list_elements:64,max_tree_nodes:64,max_tree_depth:32};\n    let core=bridge::from_program_bounded(&p,&budget).unwrap_or_else(|_|panic!(\"bounded original source copy\"));\n    let (bounds,schema)=layout();let owner=host_owner_engine();\n    let admitted=tooling(owner.admit(&core,&bounds,&schema));\n    let mut image=tooling(owner.admit_run(&admitted,&RunIntC::Nat(4096),&RunIntC::Nat(64),&FinanceInput::Absent));\n    let initial=co::capture(&admitted,&image).unwrap_or_else(|_|panic!(\"actual initial snapshot\"));\n    if ordinary_probes {\n        distinct_program_cache_contrast(&initial);\n        let gap=rp::ReferenceSource::new(factorial(3),&initial).err().expect(\"different valid source cannot associate\");\n        match gap {\n            // Category is independently specified. Exact section/row is API\n            // diagnostic data, not an independently bound source-ID oracle.\n            rp::ProjectionGap::SourceAssociation{section,row}=>{\n                assert!(!section.is_empty());assert!(row<initial.admission.view.expressions.len());\n            },\n            other=>panic!(\"ordinary source mismatch category: {other:?}\"),\n        }\n    }\n    let source=rp::ReferenceSource::new(p.clone(),&initial).expect(\"complete source association\");\n    let mut projection=rp::ReferencePrefixProjection::new(p.clone(),&initial,4096).expect(\"initial reference projection\");\n    let mut cache=wp::WitnessRecordCache::default();let mut previous=initial.clone();\n    let mut spans=Vec::new();let mut raw_count=0usize;let mut probed_incomplete=false;\n    let mut sink=|step:&wp::StrategyObservedStep| {\n        let mut stop_this=false;\n        assert_eq!(step.before.raw,previous);\n        let before_variants=variants(&step.before);let after_variants=variants(&step.after);\n        match &step.observed {\n            co::ObservedStep::Event(record)=>{\n                assert_eq!(record.before,step.before.raw);assert_eq!(record.after,step.after.raw);\n                raw_count+=1;\n                let prior_reference=projection.returned().clone();\n                match projection.push(record).expect(\"actual B to A boundary/interval translation\") {\n                    rp::ProjectionProgress::Pending{raw}=>{\n                        assert_eq!(raw,*record);assert_eq!(projection.returned(),&prior_reference);\n                        if ordinary_probes && !probed_incomplete && record.event.event_kind==EventKind::HelperEnter {\n                            assert_eq!(projection.finish().unwrap_err(),rp::ProjectionGap::IncompleteInterval);\n                            assert!(!projection.pending_records().is_empty());\n                            assert_eq!(projection.pending_records().last(),Some(record));\n                            for pair in projection.pending_records().windows(2) {assert_eq!(pair[0].after,pair[1].before);}\n                            assert_eq!(projection.returned(),&prior_reference);\n                            probed_incomplete=true;stop_this=true;\n                        }\n                    },\n                    rp::ProjectionProgress::Complete(span)=>{\n                        assert_eq!(span.b_start,spans.last().map_or(0,|s:&rp::ReferenceSpan|s.b_end_exclusive));\n                        assert_eq!(span.b_end_exclusive,raw_count);\n                        assert_eq!(span.raw.len(),span.b_end_exclusive-span.b_start);\n                        assert!(span.source_event>=span.b_start&&span.source_event<span.b_end_exclusive);\n                        let origin=&span.raw[span.source_event-span.b_start].event;\n                        assert!(matches!(origin.event_kind,EventKind::LegacyComplete|EventKind::Publish));\n                        let occurrence=span.raw[0].before.admission.view.occurrences.get(origin.source_expr_id).expect(\"real source occurrence row\");\n                        let path_end=occurrence.path.start.checked_add(occurrence.path.len).expect(\"actual occurrence span\");\n                        let path=&span.raw[0].before.admission.view.occurrence_paths[occurrence.path.start..path_end];\n                        assert_eq!(origin.source_occurrence,LocatorC::Occurrence{owner_is_function:occurrence.owner_is_function,function:occurrence.function,ast_path:path.to_vec()});\n                        // No B ordinal/helper count is manufactured from A work.\n                        // All source events and counters remain in span.raw.\n                        for decoded in &after_variants {\n                            let actual=rp::project_reference_boundary(&source,&step.after.raw,decoded,4096,span.reference.after.remaining_fuel).expect(\"cached boundary projection\");\n                            let rp::ReferenceBoundary::Complete{reference,..}=actual else {panic!(\"completed semantic boundary\")};\n                            assert_eq!(reference,span.reference.after);\n                        }\n                        if span.raw.len()==1 {\n                            for decoded in &before_variants {\n                                let actual=rp::project_reference_boundary(&source,&step.before.raw,decoded,4096,span.reference.before.remaining_fuel).expect(\"before variant projection\");\n                                let rp::ReferenceBoundary::Complete{reference,..}=actual else {panic!(\"complete source-before\")};\n                                assert_eq!(reference,span.reference.before);\n                            }\n                        }\n                        spans.push(span);\n                    }\n                }\n            },\n            co::ObservedStep::Terminal{before,after}=>{\n                assert_eq!(before,after);assert_eq!(before,&step.before.raw);assert_eq!(after,&step.after.raw);\n                assert_eq!(before_variants,after_variants);\n            }\n        }\n        previous=step.after.raw.clone();\n        if stop_this {wp::StreamAction::Stop}else{wp::StreamAction::Continue}\n    };\n    let first=wp::stream_owner_steps(&admitted,&mut image,Some(&mut cache),&mut sink)\n        .unwrap_or_else(|_|panic!(\"single actual owner stream\"));\n    if ordinary_probes {\n        assert_eq!(first,wp::StreamStop::Sink);\n        // Continue the SAME admitted image and record cache, without replay.\n        let resumed=wp::stream_owner_steps(&admitted,&mut image,Some(&mut cache),&mut sink)\n            .unwrap_or_else(|_|panic!(\"same-image pending helper continuation\"));\n        assert_eq!(resumed,wp::StreamStop::Terminal);\n    }else{assert_eq!(first,wp::StreamStop::Terminal);}\n    drop(sink);\n    assert_eq!(probed_incomplete,ordinary_probes);\n    let returned=co::capture(&admitted,&image).unwrap_or_else(|_|panic!(\"actual returned boundary\"));\n    assert_eq!(returned,previous);assert!(matches!(returned.image.outcome,OutcomeC::Halted{..}));\n    let final_reference=projection.finish().expect(\"no omitted trailing helper interval\");\n    assert!(projection.pending_records().is_empty());\n    assert_eq!(spans.iter().map(|s|s.raw.len()).sum::<usize>(),raw_count);\n    assert_eq!(projection.records().len(),spans.len());\n    let mut states=vec![projection.initial().clone()];\n    for (i,r) in projection.records().iter().enumerate() {\n        assert_eq!(&r.before,&states[i]);states.push(r.after.clone());\n    }\n    assert_eq!(states.last(),Some(final_reference));\n    if ordinary_probes {compare_b0_schedule(&initial,&spans);}\n    let snapshots=states.iter().map(snapshot).collect::<Vec<_>>();\n    let records=projection.records().iter().enumerate().map(|(i,r)|json!({\"rule_start_line\":r.rule_start_line,\"charge\":r.charge,\"before_snapshot\":i,\"after_snapshot\":i+1})).collect::<Vec<_>>();\n    let work=states.iter().map(|s|s.initial_fuel.checked_sub(s.remaining_fuel).expect(\"reference work invariant\")).collect::<Vec<_>>();\n    let charged:u128=projection.records().iter().map(|r|r.charge as u128).sum();\n    assert_eq!(work.last().copied(),Some(charged));\n    let actual=json!({\"complete_program\":program(&p),\"snapshots\":snapshots,\"records\":records,\"prefix_work_A\":work,\"charged_A_work\":charged,\"A_event_count\":projection.records().len(),\"terminal_outcome\":outcome(&final_reference.outcome),\"logical_depth_peak_A\":states.iter().map(|s|s.frames.len()).max().unwrap()});\n    let expected:J=serde_json::from_str(frozen).expect(\"independently frozen full prefix fixture\");\n    for key in [\"complete_program\",\"snapshots\",\"records\",\"prefix_work_A\",\"charged_A_work\",\"A_event_count\",\"terminal_outcome\",\"logical_depth_peak_A\"] {\n        assert!(expected.get(key).is_some(),\"missing independent field {key}\");\n        assert_eq!(&actual[key],&expected[key],\"complete independent reference field {key}\");\n    }\n    // Raw B work is retained above; it is deliberately not compared to A fuel.\n    assert_eq!(spans.last().expect(\"publication span\").raw.last().unwrap().after,returned);\n}\n\n// This existing independently frozen contrast predates the new consumer source.\nconst FACT2: &str = include_str!(\"/home/charl/Moriarty/.moriarty-dev/runtime/sherlock-review-20261017/UIREQ035-independent-reference-prefix-oracle-20261018/expectations/factorial2-normal-program-contrast-A39-prefix.json\");\n\n// A valid distinct program is admitted/captured only; no old owner step is run.\nfn capture_initial(p:&a::Program)->co::HostSnapshot {\n    let budget=bridge::SourceCopyBudget{max_functions:4,max_parameters_per_function:8,max_total_parameters:8,max_expr_nodes:128,max_copy_depth:32,max_match_arms:16,max_name_bytes:512,max_list_elements:64,max_tree_nodes:64,max_tree_depth:32};\n    let core=bridge::from_program_bounded(p,&budget).unwrap_or_else(|_|panic!(\"bounded valid contrast source\"));\n    let (bounds,schema)=layout();let owner=host_owner_engine();\n    let admitted=tooling(owner.admit(&core,&bounds,&schema));\n    let image=tooling(owner.admit_run(&admitted,&RunIntC::Nat(4096),&RunIntC::Nat(64),&FinanceInput::Absent));\n    co::capture(&admitted,&image).unwrap_or_else(|_|panic!(\"valid actual initial capture\"))\n}\nfn distinct_program_cache_contrast(initial:&co::HostSnapshot) {\n    let seed=capture_initial(&factorial(3));\n    assert_ne!(seed.admission.view,initial.admission.view);\n    let seed_plan=wp::construct_plan(&seed).expect(\"valid seed plan\");\n    let actual_plan=wp::construct_plan(initial).expect(\"valid contrast plan\");\n    let mut cache=wp::WitnessCache::default();\n    let seed_cold=wp::evaluate_memoized(&seed_plan,&seed,&mut cache,wp::SlotStorage::RetainAll).expect(\"initial-only seed\");\n    assert!(seed_cold.scheduling.scope_reset);\n    let changed=wp::evaluate_memoized(&actual_plan,initial,&mut cache,wp::SlotStorage::LastUse).expect(\"exact changed program scope\");\n    assert!(changed.scheduling.scope_reset);assert_eq!(changed.scheduling.cache_hits,0);\n    let baseline=wp::evaluate_uncached(&actual_plan,initial).expect(\"actual contrast baseline\");\n    assert_eq!(changed.witness.decoded,baseline.decoded);\n    let warm=wp::evaluate_memoized(&actual_plan,initial,&mut cache,wp::SlotStorage::LastUse).expect(\"same exact contrast scope\");\n    assert!(!warm.scheduling.scope_reset);assert_eq!(warm.scheduling.cache_misses,0);\n    assert_eq!(warm.witness.decoded,baseline.decoded);\n}\n\nconst LET_LEAF_VAR: &str = include_str!(\"/home/charl/Moriarty/.moriarty-dev/runtime/sherlock-review-20261017/UIREQ035-independent-normal-countercase-oracle-20261018/expectations/let-leaf-pattern-var-complete-A39-prefix.json\");\nfn let_leaf_pattern_var()->Arc<a::Program> {\n    let held=Arc::new(a::Expr::Let(\"x\".into(),uint(3),Arc::new(a::Expr::Unary(a::UnaryOp::Leaf,var(\"x\")))));\n    Arc::new(a::Program{functions:vec![],entry:Arc::new(a::Expr::Match(held,vec![a::Arm{pattern:a::Pattern::Var(\"whole\".into()),body:var(\"whole\")}]))})\n}\n#[test]\nfn factorial_two_complete_prefix_program_cache_and_incomplete_stream(){exercise(factorial(2),FACT2,true);}\n#[test]\nfn let_leaf_pattern_variable_complete_reference_prefix(){exercise(let_leaf_pattern_var(),LET_LEAF_VAR,false);}\n\n// Real B counters are read from the saved owner observations. None of these\n// counters is computed from A charges, expected rows or a reconstructed engine.\nfn verify_record_counters(record:&co::CompleteStepRecord) {\n    let before=&record.before.image;let after=&record.after.image;let event=&record.event;\n    assert_eq!(after.run_id,before.run_id);assert_eq!(after.initial_fuel,before.initial_fuel);\n    assert_eq!(after.consumed_work,before.consumed_work.checked_add(event.work_delta as u128).expect(\"B work addition\"));\n    assert_eq!(after.helper_work,before.helper_work.checked_add(event.helper_work_delta as u128).expect(\"B helper work addition\"));\n    assert_eq!(after.helper_visits,before.helper_visits.checked_add(event.helper_visits_delta as u128).expect(\"B helper visits addition\"));\n    assert_eq!(after.reference_cursor,before.reference_cursor.checked_add(event.reference_cursor_delta as u128).expect(\"B reference cursor addition\"));\n    assert_eq!(after.remaining_work.checked_add(event.work_delta as u128),Some(before.remaining_work));\n    assert_eq!(after.remaining_work.checked_add(after.consumed_work),Some(after.initial_fuel));\n    assert_eq!(event.outcome_payload,after.outcome);\n}\n\n// Entire public normative inventory formatting, not selected schedule metadata.\nfn b_rule_id(rule:RuleIdC)->&'static str {match rule {\n    RuleIdC::KMachineEvalLiteralValid=>\"k.machine.eval.literal.valid\",\n    RuleIdC::KMachineEvalLiteralInvalid=>\"k.machine.eval.literal.invalid\",\n    RuleIdC::KMachineEvalVariablePresent=>\"k.machine.eval.variable.present\",\n    RuleIdC::KMachineEvalVariableAbsent=>\"k.machine.eval.variable.absent\",\n    RuleIdC::KMachineEvalLet=>\"k.machine.eval.let\",\n    RuleIdC::KMachineEvalBinary=>\"k.machine.eval.binary\",\n    RuleIdC::KMachineEvalUnary=>\"k.machine.eval.unary\",\n    RuleIdC::KMachineEvalIf=>\"k.machine.eval.if\",\n    RuleIdC::KMachineEvalMatch=>\"k.machine.eval.match\",\n    RuleIdC::KMachineEvalCallEmpty=>\"k.machine.eval.call.empty\",\n    RuleIdC::KMachineEvalCallArguments=>\"k.machine.eval.call.arguments\",\n    RuleIdC::KMachinePushAccept=>\"k.machine.push.accept\",\n    RuleIdC::KMachinePushRefuse=>\"k.machine.push.refuse\",\n    RuleIdC::KMachineReturnLet=>\"k.machine.return.let\",\n    RuleIdC::KMachineReturnLeft=>\"k.machine.return.left\",\n    RuleIdC::KMachineReturnRight=>\"k.machine.return.right\",\n    RuleIdC::KMachineReturnUnary=>\"k.machine.return.unary\",\n    RuleIdC::KMachineReturnIfTrue=>\"k.machine.return.if.true\",\n    RuleIdC::KMachineReturnIfFalse=>\"k.machine.return.if.false\",\n    RuleIdC::KMachineReturnIfInvalid=>\"k.machine.return.if.invalid\",\n    RuleIdC::KMachineReturnMatch=>\"k.machine.return.match\",\n    RuleIdC::KMachineReturnArgumentsNext=>\"k.machine.return.arguments.next\",\n    RuleIdC::KMachineReturnArgumentsFinal=>\"k.machine.return.arguments.final\",\n    RuleIdC::KMachineReturnCallValid=>\"k.machine.return.call.valid\",\n    RuleIdC::KMachineReturnCallInvalid=>\"k.machine.return.call.invalid\",\n    RuleIdC::KMachineReturnScope=>\"k.machine.return.scope\",\n    RuleIdC::KMachineInvokeFind=>\"k.machine.invoke.find\",\n    RuleIdC::KMachineEnterMissing=>\"k.machine.enter.missing\",\n    RuleIdC::KMachineEnterBind=>\"k.machine.enter.bind\",\n    RuleIdC::KMachineBoundInvalid=>\"k.machine.bound.invalid\",\n    RuleIdC::KMachineBoundValid=>\"k.machine.bound.valid\",\n    RuleIdC::KMachineCasesEmpty=>\"k.machine.cases.empty\",\n    RuleIdC::KMachineCasesTry=>\"k.machine.cases.try\",\n    RuleIdC::KMachineCasesMiss=>\"k.machine.cases.miss\",\n    RuleIdC::KMachineCasesHit=>\"k.machine.cases.hit\",\n    RuleIdC::KMachinePrimitiveValue=>\"k.machine.primitive.value\",\n    RuleIdC::KMachinePrimitiveError=>\"k.machine.primitive.error\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperScalarEntry=>\"b.helper.Scalar.entry\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperScalarTag=>\"b.helper.Scalar.tag\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperScalarArithmetic=>\"b.helper.Scalar.arithmetic\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperScalarConstruct=>\"b.helper.Scalar.construct\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperScalarExit=>\"b.helper.Scalar.exit\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperScalarFailure=>\"b.helper.Scalar.failure\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperEnvGetEntry=>\"b.helper.EnvGet.entry\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperEnvGetCell=>\"b.helper.EnvGet.cell\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperEnvGetEmpty=>\"b.helper.EnvGet.empty\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperEnvGetExit=>\"b.helper.EnvGet.exit\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperEnvGetFailure=>\"b.helper.EnvGet.failure\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperEnvPutEntry=>\"b.helper.EnvPut.entry\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperEnvPutCell=>\"b.helper.EnvPut.cell\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperEnvPutInsert=>\"b.helper.EnvPut.insert\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperEnvPutEmpty=>\"b.helper.EnvPut.empty\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperEnvPutExit=>\"b.helper.EnvPut.exit\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperEnvPutFailure=>\"b.helper.EnvPut.failure\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperFindEntry=>\"b.helper.Find.entry\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperFindRow=>\"b.helper.Find.row\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperFindEmpty=>\"b.helper.Find.empty\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperFindExit=>\"b.helper.Find.exit\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperFindFailure=>\"b.helper.Find.failure\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperBindEntry=>\"b.helper.Bind.entry\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperBindPair=>\"b.helper.Bind.pair\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperBindEmpty=>\"b.helper.Bind.empty\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperBindArity=>\"b.helper.Bind.arity\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperBindType=>\"b.helper.Bind.type\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperBindDuplicate=>\"b.helper.Bind.duplicate\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperBindInsert=>\"b.helper.Bind.insert\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperBindPropagate=>\"b.helper.Bind.propagate\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperBindExit=>\"b.helper.Bind.exit\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperBindFailure=>\"b.helper.Bind.failure\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperAppendEntry=>\"b.helper.Append.entry\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperAppendCell=>\"b.helper.Append.cell\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperAppendEmpty=>\"b.helper.Append.empty\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperAppendTail=>\"b.helper.Append.tail\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperAppendCopy=>\"b.helper.Append.copy\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperAppendExit=>\"b.helper.Append.exit\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperAppendFailure=>\"b.helper.Append.failure\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperValidateEntry=>\"b.helper.Validate.entry\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperValidateOccurrence=>\"b.helper.Validate.occurrence\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperValidateField=>\"b.helper.Validate.field\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperValidateDeclaration=>\"b.helper.Validate.declaration\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperValidateEmpty=>\"b.helper.Validate.empty\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperValidateInvalid=>\"b.helper.Validate.invalid\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperValidateExit=>\"b.helper.Validate.exit\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperValidateFailure=>\"b.helper.Validate.failure\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperEqualEntry=>\"b.helper.Equal.entry\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperEqualPair=>\"b.helper.Equal.pair\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperEqualField=>\"b.helper.Equal.field\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperEqualEmpty=>\"b.helper.Equal.empty\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperEqualDifferent=>\"b.helper.Equal.different\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperEqualExit=>\"b.helper.Equal.exit\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperEqualFailure=>\"b.helper.Equal.failure\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperMatchEntry=>\"b.helper.Match.entry\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperMatchArm=>\"b.helper.Match.arm\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperMatchOccurrence=>\"b.helper.Match.occurrence\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperMatchField=>\"b.helper.Match.field\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperMatchBinding=>\"b.helper.Match.binding\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperMatchDistinct=>\"b.helper.Match.distinct\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperMatchDiscard=>\"b.helper.Match.discard\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperMatchNext=>\"b.helper.Match.next\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperMatchSelected=>\"b.helper.Match.selected\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperMatchEmpty=>\"b.helper.Match.empty\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperMatchExit=>\"b.helper.Match.exit\",\n    RuleIdC::BHelperMatchFailure=>\"b.helper.Match.failure\",\n    RuleIdC::BBookkeepingTaskEnqueue=>\"b.bookkeeping.task.enqueue\",\n    RuleIdC::BBookkeepingTaskRelease=>\"b.bookkeeping.task.release\",\n    RuleIdC::BBookkeepingResumeStore=>\"b.bookkeeping.resume.store\",\n    RuleIdC::BBookkeepingResumeRestore=>\"b.bookkeeping.resume.restore\",\n    RuleIdC::KAdminStartupValid=>\"k.admin.startup.valid\",\n    RuleIdC::KAdminStartupInvalid=>\"k.admin.startup.invalid\",\n    RuleIdC::KAdminPublishValue=>\"k.admin.publish.value\",\n    RuleIdC::KAdminPublishError=>\"k.admin.publish.error\",\n    RuleIdC::KAdminPublishExhausted=>\"k.admin.publish.exhausted\",\n}}\nconst FACT2_B0: &str = include_str!(\"/home/charl/Moriarty/.moriarty-dev/runtime/sherlock-review-20261017/UIREQ035-independent-B0-work-oracle-20261018/factorial2-normal-program-contrast-A39-prefix-B0-clocks.json\");\nfn b_clock_row(a_record:Option<usize>,preceding_rule:Option<&str>,raw:&co::HostSnapshot,semantic_index:usize)->J {\n    let image=&raw.image;\n    json!([a_record,preceding_rule,image.consumed_work,image.helper_work,image.helper_visits,image.reference_cursor,image.remaining_work,semantic_index])\n}\nfn compare_b0_schedule(initial:&co::HostSnapshot,spans:&[rp::ReferenceSpan]) {\n    // Construct the COMPLETE actual prefix first; no expected cell supplies any\n    // field, rule, counter, missing interval or semantic association.\n    let columns=json!([\"A_record_index_or_null\",\"preceding_B_rule_id_or_null\",\"consumed_work\",\"helper_work\",\"helper_visits\",\"reference_cursor\",\"remaining_work\",\"erased_semantic_A_snapshot_index\"]);\n    let mut prefixes=vec![b_clock_row(None,None,initial,0)];let mut intervals=Vec::new();\n    let mut previous=initial.clone();let mut ordinal=0usize;\n    for (a_index,span) in spans.iter().enumerate() {\n        assert_eq!(span.b_start,ordinal);\n        assert_eq!(span.raw.len(),span.b_end_exclusive-span.b_start);\n        assert_eq!(span.source_event.checked_add(1),Some(span.b_end_exclusive),\"normal B0 separate completion ends interval\");\n        let mut helper_ids=Vec::new();let mut completion_id=None;\n        for (offset,record) in span.raw.iter().enumerate() {\n            assert_eq!(record.before,previous);verify_record_counters(record);\n            let id=b_rule_id(record.event.rule_id);let is_completion=span.b_start+offset==span.source_event;\n            if is_completion {\n                assert!(matches!(record.event.event_kind,EventKind::LegacyComplete|EventKind::Publish));\n                completion_id=Some(id);\n            }else{\n                assert!(!matches!(record.event.event_kind,EventKind::LegacyComplete|EventKind::Publish));\n                // Charged bookkeeping belongs here as well; event kind cannot\n                // hide any prefix row or charged preceding rule.\n                if record.event.work_delta!=0 {helper_ids.push(id);}\n            }\n            prefixes.push(b_clock_row(Some(a_index),Some(id),&record.after,if is_completion {a_index+1}else{a_index}));\n            previous=record.after.clone();ordinal+=1;\n        }\n        intervals.push(json!({\"A_record_index\":a_index,\"A_rule_line\":span.reference.rule_start_line,\"first_B_record\":span.b_start,\"B_records_exclusive\":span.b_end_exclusive,\"helper_rule_ids\":helper_ids,\"legacy_rule_id\":completion_id.expect(\"actual source completion\")}));\n    }\n    assert_eq!(prefixes.len(),ordinal+1);\n    let actual=json!({\"clockPrefixColumns\":columns,\"clockPrefixes\":prefixes,\"intervals\":intervals});\n    // B0 describes this explicit DedicatedSorts run. No A/B work equality is\n    // asserted; the previous full A39 comparison remains independently bound.\n    let profile=match initial.admission.identity.profile_id {2=>\"sherlock-helper-microstep/1\",_=>panic!(\"selected B profile\")};\n    let grammar=format!(\"{:?}\",initial.admission.identity.grammar_domain);\n    let expected:J=serde_json::from_str(FACT2_B0).expect(\"opaque independent complete B0 schedule\");\n    assert_eq!(expected.get(\"profile\"),Some(&json!(profile)));\n    assert_eq!(expected.get(\"grammarDomain\"),Some(&json!(grammar)));\n    assert_eq!(expected.get(\"initialFuel\"),Some(&json!(initial.image.initial_fuel)));\n    for key in [\"clockPrefixColumns\",\"clockPrefixes\",\"intervals\"] {\n        assert!(expected.get(key).is_some(),\"missing independent B0 field {key}\");\n        assert_eq!(&actual[key],&expected[key],\"complete independent B0 field {key}\");\n    }\n}\n\n=== END FULL BODY 02-full-new-consumer ===\n\n=== BEGIN FULL BODY 03-full-consumed-projector | /home/charl/Moriarty/.moriarty-dev/runtime/sherlock-review-20261017/witness-reference-projection-ordinary-QA-20261018/snapshot/crates/mori-core/src/sherlock/helper_machine/reference_projection.rs | 24000 bytes | SHA256 ad197ca8b1b965d7b29af16daa629c399cf5d19f9c6566105a65945546c61547 ===\n//! Read-only semantic reference projection of saved, actual B observations.\n//!\n//! No source/owner step is evaluated here. The caller retains the exact original\n//! A syntax; all held expressions/functions/arms are associated with actual B\n//! occurrence/table rows. This is trusted host diagnostics, not authentication,\n//! canonical physical projection, state import, admission or ProjectRel/Link.\n//! Raw B snapshots and helper intervals remain available separately. A logical\n//! reference fuel input is explicit; B remaining/helper work is never renamed A\n//! fuel. Unmapped/incomplete/resource-divergent observations return typed gaps.\nuse super::complete_observation::{AdmissionSnapshot, CompleteStepRecord, ExpressionSnapshot, HostSnapshot};\nuse super::shared::*;\nuse super::witness_plan::{self as wp, DecodedPayload, DecodedSnapshot, DecodedValue, InputValue, SlotValue, ValueNode};\nuse crate::sherlock as a;\nuse std::collections::BTreeMap;\nuse std::sync::Arc;\n\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub enum ProjectionGap {\n    Witness(wp::WitnessFailure),\n    SourceAssociation { section: &'static str, row: usize },\n    MissingField(&'static str),\n    WrongPayload(&'static str),\n    UnrepresentableValue,\n    UnsupportedNominalType(usize),\n    ReferenceFuel,\n    AdmissionChanged,\n    Discontinuity,\n    UnmappedRule(RuleIdC),\n    UnappliedSourceRule,\n    IncompleteInterval,\n    BResourceOutcome,\n}\ntype Result<T> = std::result::Result<T, ProjectionGap>;\nfn source_gap(section: &'static str, row: usize) -> ProjectionGap {\n    ProjectionGap::SourceAssociation { section, row }\n}\nfn bin(op: BinaryOp) -> a::BinaryOp { match op {\n    BinaryOp::Add => a::BinaryOp::Add, BinaryOp::Sub => a::BinaryOp::Sub,\n    BinaryOp::Mul => a::BinaryOp::Mul, BinaryOp::Eq => a::BinaryOp::Eq,\n    BinaryOp::Lt => a::BinaryOp::Lt, BinaryOp::Cons => a::BinaryOp::Cons,\n    BinaryOp::Branch => a::BinaryOp::Branch,\n} }\nfn unary(op: UnaryOp) -> a::UnaryOp { match op {\n    UnaryOp::Leaf => a::UnaryOp::Leaf, UnaryOp::Not => a::UnaryOp::Not,\n} }\nfn ty(id: TypeIdC) -> Result<a::Type> { Ok(match id.0 {\n    0 => a::Type::UInt, 1 => a::Type::Bool, 2 => a::Type::List, 3 => a::Type::Tree,\n    n => return Err(ProjectionGap::UnsupportedNominalType(n)),\n}) }\nfn field<'a>(fields: &'a [wp::NamedValue], name: &'static str) -> Result<&'a SlotValue> {\n    fields.iter().find(|f| f.field == name).map(|f| &f.value).ok_or(ProjectionGap::MissingField(name))\n}\nfn payload<'a>(value: &'a SlotValue, name: &'static str) -> Result<&'a DecodedPayload> {\n    if let SlotValue::Payload(p) = value { Ok(p) } else { Err(ProjectionGap::WrongPayload(name)) }\n}\nfn sequence<'a>(value: &'a SlotValue, name: &'static str) -> Result<&'a [SlotValue]> {\n    if let SlotValue::Sequence { items, .. } = value { Ok(items) } else { Err(ProjectionGap::WrongPayload(name)) }\n}\n/// Convert the existing flat, fully resolved witness value; no AST evaluation.\npub fn reference_value(value: &DecodedValue) -> Result<a::Value> {\n    let mut nodes: Vec<a::Value> = Vec::with_capacity(value.nodes.len());\n    for row in &value.nodes {\n        let child = |i: usize| nodes.get(i).cloned().ok_or(ProjectionGap::UnrepresentableValue);\n        let result = match *row {\n            ValueNode::UInt(n) => a::Value::UInt(n), ValueNode::Bool(b) => a::Value::Bool(b),\n            ValueNode::Nil => a::Value::List(Vec::new()),\n            ValueNode::Cons { head, tail } => {\n                let (a::Value::UInt(n), a::Value::List(tail)) = (child(head)?, child(tail)?) else { return Err(ProjectionGap::UnrepresentableValue); };\n                let mut list = Vec::with_capacity(tail.len() + 1); list.push(n); list.extend(tail); a::Value::List(list)\n            }\n            ValueNode::Leaf { value } => {\n                let a::Value::UInt(n) = child(value)? else { return Err(ProjectionGap::UnrepresentableValue); };\n                a::Value::Tree(a::Tree::Leaf(n))\n            }\n            ValueNode::Branch { left, right } => {\n                let (a::Value::Tree(l), a::Value::Tree(r)) = (child(left)?, child(right)?) else { return Err(ProjectionGap::UnrepresentableValue); };\n                a::Value::Tree(a::Tree::Branch(Arc::new(l), Arc::new(r)))\n            }\n            ValueNode::U128OutOfRange => return Err(ProjectionGap::UnrepresentableValue),\n        };\n        nodes.push(result);\n    }\n    nodes.get(value.root).cloned().ok_or(ProjectionGap::UnrepresentableValue)\n}\nfn value(slot: &SlotValue) -> Result<a::Value> {\n    if let SlotValue::Value(v) = slot { reference_value(v) } else { Err(ProjectionGap::WrongPayload(\"value\")) }\n}\nfn values(slot: &SlotValue) -> Result<Vec<a::Value>> {\n    sequence(slot, \"values\")?.iter().map(value).collect()\n}\n/// A's map meaning keeps the first visible name in the exact newest-first B\n/// chain. Shadowed cells remain in the caller's complete raw/decoded snapshot.\nfn environment(slot: &SlotValue) -> Result<a::Environment> {\n    let SlotValue::Environment(entries) = slot else { return Err(ProjectionGap::WrongPayload(\"environment\")); };\n    let mut result = BTreeMap::new();\n    for entry in entries {\n        if !result.contains_key(&entry.name) { result.insert(entry.name.clone(), reference_value(&entry.value)?); }\n    }\n    Ok(result)\n}\n\n/// Retained exact source syntax associated with full observed program rows.\n/// Source association is a tooling comparison, not a security/source theorem.\npub struct ReferenceSource {\n    program: Arc<a::Program>, admission: AdmissionSnapshot,\n    expressions: Vec<a::ExprRef>, arms: Vec<a::Arm>,\n}\nimpl ReferenceSource {\n    pub fn new(program: Arc<a::Program>, initial: &HostSnapshot) -> Result<Self> {\n        let view = &initial.admission.view;\n        if view.expressions.len() != view.occurrences.len() || view.functions.len() != program.functions.len() {\n            return Err(source_gap(\"program\", 0));\n        }\n        let mut expressions = Vec::with_capacity(view.expressions.len());\n        for (id, occurrence) in view.occurrences.iter().enumerate() {\n            let mut expr = if occurrence.owner_is_function {\n                program.functions.get(occurrence.function).ok_or(source_gap(\"function\", id))?.body.clone()\n            } else {\n                if occurrence.function != 0 { return Err(source_gap(\"entry\", id)); }\n                program.entry.clone()\n            };\n            let end = occurrence.path.start.checked_add(occurrence.path.len).ok_or(source_gap(\"path\", id))?;\n            let path = view.occurrence_paths.get(occurrence.path.start..end).ok_or(source_gap(\"path\", id))?;\n            for &index in path {\n                expr = match expr.as_ref() {\n                    a::Expr::Let(_, x, y) | a::Expr::Binary(_, x, y) => match index { 0 => x.clone(), 1 => y.clone(), _ => return Err(source_gap(\"path\", id)) },\n                    a::Expr::Unary(_, x) if index == 0 => x.clone(),\n                    a::Expr::If(x,y,z) => match index { 0=>x.clone(),1=>y.clone(),2=>z.clone(),_=>return Err(source_gap(\"path\",id)) },\n                    a::Expr::Call(_, args) => args.get(index).cloned().ok_or(source_gap(\"call path\", id))?,\n                    a::Expr::Match(x, arms) => if index == 0 { x.clone() } else { arms.get(index-1).ok_or(source_gap(\"arm path\", id))?.body.clone() },\n                    _ => return Err(source_gap(\"path\", id)),\n                };\n            }\n            expressions.push(expr);\n        }\n        let materialized = wp::materialize(initial).map_err(ProjectionGap::Witness)?;\n        let constants = sequence(field(&materialized.evaluation.decoded.fields,\"constants\")?,\"constants\")?;\n        let mut arms: Vec<Option<a::Arm>> = vec![None; view.arms.len()];\n        let mut result = Self { program, admission: initial.admission.clone(), expressions, arms: Vec::new() };\n        for (i, row) in view.expressions.iter().enumerate() {\n            let source = result.expr(i)?;\n            let equal = match (row,source.as_ref()) {\n                (ExpressionSnapshot::Literal {constant}, a::Expr::Literal(v)) => value(constants.get(*constant).ok_or(source_gap(\"constant\",i))?)? == *v,\n                (ExpressionSnapshot::Var {binder}, a::Expr::Var(n)) => result.name(*binder)? == *n,\n                (ExpressionSnapshot::Let {binder,value,body},a::Expr::Let(n,x,y)) => result.name(*binder)? == *n && result.expr(*value)? == *x && result.expr(*body)? == *y,\n                (ExpressionSnapshot::Binary {op,left,right},a::Expr::Binary(o,x,y)) => bin(*op)==*o && result.expr(*left)?==*x && result.expr(*right)?==*y,\n                (ExpressionSnapshot::Unary {op,operand},a::Expr::Unary(o,x)) => unary(*op)==*o && result.expr(*operand)?==*x,\n                (ExpressionSnapshot::If {cond,then_expr,else_expr},a::Expr::If(x,y,z)) => result.expr(*cond)?==*x && result.expr(*then_expr)?==*y && result.expr(*else_expr)?==*z,\n                (ExpressionSnapshot::Call {function_name,args},a::Expr::Call(n,xs)) => result.name(*function_name)?==*n && result.exprs(*args)?==*xs,\n                (ExpressionSnapshot::Match {scrutinee,arms: slice},a::Expr::Match(x,source_arms)) => {\n                    if result.expr(*scrutinee)? != *x || slice.len != source_arms.len() { false } else {\n                        for (offset, arm) in source_arms.iter().enumerate() {\n                            let at = slice.start.checked_add(offset).ok_or(source_gap(\"arms\",i))?;\n                            let row = view.arms.get(at).ok_or(source_gap(\"arms\",at))?;\n                            if result.expr(row.body)? != arm.body || result.pattern(row.pattern)? != arm.pattern { return Err(source_gap(\"arms\",at)); }\n                            if let Some(previous) = &arms[at] { if previous != arm { return Err(source_gap(\"arm sharing\",at)); } }\n                            arms[at] = Some(arm.clone());\n                        }\n                        true\n                    }\n                }\n                _ => false,\n            };\n            if !equal { return Err(source_gap(\"expression\",i)); }\n        }\n        result.arms = arms.into_iter().enumerate().map(|(i,x)|x.ok_or(source_gap(\"unassociated arm\",i))).collect::<Result<_>>()?;\n        for (i,(row, function)) in view.functions.iter().zip(&result.program.functions).enumerate() {\n            if result.name(row.function_name)?!=function.name || ty(row.return_type)?!=function.return_type || result.expr(row.body)?!=function.body || row.params.len!=function.parameters.len() {\n                return Err(source_gap(\"function\",i));\n            }\n            for (offset,parameter) in function.parameters.iter().enumerate() {\n                let index=row.params.start.checked_add(offset).ok_or(source_gap(\"parameter\",i))?;\n                let p=view.parameters.get(index).ok_or(source_gap(\"parameter\",index))?;\n                if result.name(p.binder)?!=parameter.name || ty(p.sort)?!=parameter.ty { return Err(source_gap(\"parameter\",index)); }\n            }\n        }\n        if result.expr(view.entry)? != result.program.entry { return Err(source_gap(\"entry\",view.entry)); }\n        Ok(result)\n    }\n    fn name(&self, id: usize) -> Result<String> { self.admission.view.names.get(id).cloned().ok_or(source_gap(\"name\",id)) }\n    fn expr(&self, id: usize) -> Result<a::ExprRef> { self.expressions.get(id).cloned().ok_or(source_gap(\"expression\",id)) }\n    fn exprs(&self, slice: SliceC) -> Result<Vec<a::ExprRef>> {\n        let end=slice.start.checked_add(slice.len).ok_or(source_gap(\"children\",slice.start))?;\n        self.admission.view.children.get(slice.start..end).ok_or(source_gap(\"children\",slice.start))?.iter().map(|&i|self.expr(i)).collect()\n    }\n    fn arms(&self, slice: SliceC) -> Result<Vec<a::Arm>> {\n        let end=slice.start.checked_add(slice.len).ok_or(source_gap(\"arms\",slice.start))?;\n        self.arms.get(slice.start..end).map(|x|x.to_vec()).ok_or(source_gap(\"arms\",slice.start))\n    }\n    fn pattern(&self,id:usize)->Result<a::Pattern> { Ok(match *self.admission.view.patterns.get(id).ok_or(source_gap(\"pattern\",id))? {\n        PatternRowC::PVar{x}=>a::Pattern::Var(self.name(x)?), PatternRowC::PNil=>a::Pattern::Nil,\n        PatternRowC::PCons{x,y}=>a::Pattern::Cons(self.name(x)?,self.name(y)?), PatternRowC::PLeaf{x}=>a::Pattern::Leaf(self.name(x)?),\n        PatternRowC::PBranch{x,y}=>a::Pattern::Branch(self.name(x)?,self.name(y)?),\n    }) }\n    fn frame(&self,p:&DecodedPayload)->Result<a::Frame> {\n        let InputValue::Frame(raw)=&p.raw else { return Err(ProjectionGap::WrongPayload(\"frame\")); };\n        let get=|n|field(&p.fields,n);\n        Ok(match *raw {\n            FrameRowC::LetF{binder,body,..}=>a::Frame::Let(self.name(binder)?,self.expr(body)?,environment(get(\"saved_env\")?)?),\n            FrameRowC::LeftF{op,right,..}=>a::Frame::Left(bin(op),self.expr(right)?,environment(get(\"saved_env\")?)?),\n            FrameRowC::RightF{op,..}=>a::Frame::Right(bin(op),value(get(\"left\")?)?),\n            FrameRowC::UnaryF{op,..}=>a::Frame::Unary(unary(op)),\n            FrameRowC::IfF{then_expr,else_expr,..}=>a::Frame::If(self.expr(then_expr)?,self.expr(else_expr)?,environment(get(\"saved_env\")?)?),\n            FrameRowC::MatchF{arms,..}=>a::Frame::Match(self.arms(arms)?,environment(get(\"saved_env\")?)?),\n            FrameRowC::ArgsF{function_name,rest,..}=>a::Frame::Args(self.name(function_name)?,values(get(\"completed\")?)?,self.exprs(rest)?,environment(get(\"saved_env\")?)?),\n            FrameRowC::ReturnF{return_type,..}=>a::Frame::Return(ty(return_type)?,environment(get(\"saved_env\")?)?),\n            FrameRowC::ScopeF{..}=>a::Frame::Scope(environment(get(\"saved_env\")?)?),\n        })\n    }\n    fn control(&self,p:&DecodedPayload)->Result<a::Control> {\n        let InputValue::Control(raw)=&p.raw else { return Err(ProjectionGap::WrongPayload(\"control\")); };\n        let get=|n|field(&p.fields,n);\n        Ok(match *raw {\n            ControlC::Eval{expr}=>a::Control::Eval(self.expr(expr)?),\n            ControlC::Return{..}=>a::Control::Return(value(get(\"value\")?)?),\n            ControlC::ScheduleNext{next,..}=>a::Control::Push(self.frame(payload(get(\"frame\")?,\"frame\")?)?,Box::new(a::Control::Eval(self.expr(next)?)),environment(get(\"env\")?)?),\n            ControlC::Invoke{function_name,..}=>a::Control::Invoke(self.name(function_name)?,values(get(\"args\")?)?),\n            ControlC::Enter{function,..}=>a::Control::Enter(function.map(|i|self.program.functions.get(i).cloned().ok_or(source_gap(\"function\",i))).transpose()?,values(get(\"args\")?)?),\n            ControlC::Bound{binding,return_type,body}=>a::Control::Bound(match binding {BoundBinding::Bad=>None,BoundBinding::Ok{..}=>Some(environment(get(\"binding\")?)?)},ty(return_type)?,self.expr(body)?),\n            ControlC::Cases{arms,..}=>a::Control::Cases(value(get(\"value\")?)?,self.arms(arms)?,environment(get(\"saved_env\")?)?),\n            ControlC::CaseResult{matching,body,rest,..}=>a::Control::CaseResult(match matching {CaseMatching::NoMatch=>None,CaseMatching::Matched{..}=>Some(environment(get(\"matching\")?)?)},value(get(\"value\")?)?,self.expr(body)?,self.arms(rest)?,environment(get(\"saved_env\")?)?),\n            ControlC::PrimResult{result}=>a::Control::PrimitiveResult(match result {PrimOutcome::Value{..}=>Ok(value(get(\"value\")?)?),PrimOutcome::Error{code}=>Err(code)}),\n            ControlC::Error{code}=>a::Control::Error(code),\n        })\n    }\n    fn snapshot(&self,raw:&HostSnapshot,decoded:&DecodedSnapshot,initial:u128,remaining:u128)->Result<a::Snapshot> {\n        if raw.admission!=self.admission || decoded.metadata.admission!=self.admission { return Err(ProjectionGap::AdmissionChanged); }\n        if remaining>initial { return Err(ProjectionGap::ReferenceFuel); }\n        let outcome=match raw.image.outcome {\n            OutcomeC::Running=>a::Outcome::Pending,\n            OutcomeC::Halted{..}=>a::Outcome::Done(value(field(&payload(field(&decoded.fields,\"outcome\")?,\"outcome\")?.fields,\"value\")?)?),\n            OutcomeC::Rejected{code}=>a::Outcome::Rejected(code),\n            OutcomeC::Exhausted{reason:ExhaustReason::Fuel} if remaining==0=>a::Outcome::Exhausted,\n            OutcomeC::Exhausted{..}=>return Err(ProjectionGap::BResourceOutcome),\n        };\n        let control=if outcome==a::Outcome::Pending {Some(self.control(payload(field(&decoded.fields,\"control\")?,\"control\")?)?)} else {None};\n        let frames=sequence(field(&decoded.fields,\"frames\")?,\"frames\")?.iter().map(|x|self.frame(payload(x,\"frame\")?)).collect::<Result<Vec<_>>>()?;\n        Ok(a::Snapshot{program:self.program.clone(),control,environment:environment(field(&decoded.fields,\"current_environment\")?)?,frames,stack_limit:raw.image.stack_limit,remaining_fuel:remaining,initial_fuel:initial,outcome})\n    }\n}\n\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub enum ReferenceBoundary {\n    Complete { reference: a::Snapshot, raw: HostSnapshot, decoded: DecodedSnapshot },\n    /// Complete phase/result/task payloads remain present, not coerced to A.\n    PendingHelper { raw: HostSnapshot, decoded: DecodedSnapshot },\n}\npub fn project_reference_boundary(source:&ReferenceSource,raw:&HostSnapshot,decoded:&DecodedSnapshot,\n    reference_initial_fuel:u128,reference_remaining_fuel:u128)->Result<ReferenceBoundary> {\n    if raw.image.helper.is_some() || raw.image.result.is_some() || !raw.image.tasks.is_empty() {\n        return Ok(ReferenceBoundary::PendingHelper{raw:raw.clone(),decoded:decoded.clone()});\n    }\n    Ok(ReferenceBoundary::Complete{reference:source.snapshot(raw,decoded,reference_initial_fuel,reference_remaining_fuel)?,raw:raw.clone(),decoded:decoded.clone()})\n}\n\n/// Explicit A39 rule/charge table from the fixed public reference source. No\n/// B helper/physical work counter is converted to A fuel by this table.\nfn reference_rule(rule:RuleIdC)->Option<(usize,u8)> {\n    use RuleIdC::*;\n    Some(match rule {\n        KMachineEvalLiteralValid=>(102,1),KMachineEvalVariablePresent=>(108,1),KMachineEvalVariableAbsent=>(111,1),\n        KMachineEvalLet=>(114,1),KMachineEvalBinary=>(117,1),KMachineEvalUnary=>(120,1),KMachineEvalIf=>(123,1),KMachineEvalMatch=>(126,1),KMachineEvalCallEmpty=>(129,1),KMachineEvalCallArguments=>(131,1),\n        KMachinePushAccept=>(135,1),KMachinePushRefuse=>(140,1),KMachineReturnLet=>(145,1),KMachineReturnLeft=>(149,1),KMachineReturnRight=>(153,1),KMachineReturnUnary=>(157,1),\n        KMachineReturnIfTrue=>(161,1),KMachineReturnIfFalse=>(165,1),KMachineReturnIfInvalid=>(169,1),KMachineReturnMatch=>(173,1),KMachineReturnArgumentsNext=>(177,1),KMachineReturnArgumentsFinal=>(181,1),\n        KMachineReturnCallValid=>(185,1),KMachineReturnCallInvalid=>(190,1),KMachineReturnScope=>(195,1),KMachineInvokeFind=>(200,1),KMachineEnterMissing=>(202,1),KMachineEnterBind=>(204,1),\n        KMachineBoundInvalid=>(206,1),KMachineBoundValid=>(208,1),KMachineCasesEmpty=>(212,1),KMachineCasesTry=>(214,1),KMachineCasesMiss=>(217,1),KMachineCasesHit=>(220,1),KMachinePrimitiveValue=>(223,1),KMachinePrimitiveError=>(225,1),\n        KAdminPublishValue=>(80,0),KAdminPublishError=>(82,0),KAdminPublishExhausted=>(84,0),_=>return None,\n    })\n}\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub struct ReferenceSpan {\n    pub b_start: usize, pub b_end_exclusive: usize, pub source_event: usize,\n    /// All actual raw micro-records, including helper/bookkeeping intermediates.\n    pub raw: Vec<CompleteStepRecord>, pub reference: a::StepRecord,\n}\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub enum ProjectionProgress {\n    Pending { raw: CompleteStepRecord },\n    Complete(ReferenceSpan),\n}\nstruct PendingCompletion { line:usize,charge:u8,source_event:usize }\n/// Stream accumulator over SAVED owner records. It never steps either machine.\npub struct ReferencePrefixProjection {\n    source: ReferenceSource, initial:a::Snapshot, returned:a::Snapshot,\n    raw_returned:HostSnapshot, records:Vec<a::StepRecord>, next_b:usize,\n    interval:Vec<CompleteStepRecord>, interval_start:usize,\n    completion:Option<PendingCompletion>,\n}\nimpl ReferencePrefixProjection {\n    pub fn new(program:Arc<a::Program>,initial:&HostSnapshot,reference_fuel:u128)->Result<Self> {\n        let source=ReferenceSource::new(program,initial)?;\n        let materialized=wp::materialize(initial).map_err(ProjectionGap::Witness)?;\n        let ReferenceBoundary::Complete{reference,..}=project_reference_boundary(&source,initial,&materialized.evaluation.decoded,reference_fuel,reference_fuel)? else {return Err(ProjectionGap::IncompleteInterval);};\n        Ok(Self{source,initial:reference.clone(),returned:reference,raw_returned:initial.clone(),records:Vec::new(),next_b:0,interval:Vec::new(),interval_start:0,completion:None})\n    }\n    pub fn initial(&self)->&a::Snapshot{&self.initial}\n    pub fn records(&self)->&[a::StepRecord]{&self.records}\n    pub fn returned(&self)->&a::Snapshot{&self.returned}\n    pub fn pending_records(&self)->&[CompleteStepRecord]{&self.interval}\n    pub fn push(&mut self,record:&CompleteStepRecord)->Result<ProjectionProgress> {\n        if record.before!=self.raw_returned {return Err(ProjectionGap::Discontinuity);}\n        if record.before.admission!=self.source.admission || record.after.admission!=self.source.admission{return Err(ProjectionGap::AdmissionChanged);}\n        let index=self.next_b;self.next_b=self.next_b.checked_add(1).ok_or(ProjectionGap::IncompleteInterval)?;\n        self.raw_returned=record.after.clone();self.interval.push(record.clone());\n        if matches!(record.event.event_kind,EventKind::LegacyComplete|EventKind::Publish) {\n            let (line,charge)=reference_rule(record.event.rule_id).ok_or(ProjectionGap::UnmappedRule(record.event.rule_id))?;\n            if self.completion.is_some(){return Err(ProjectionGap::IncompleteInterval);}\n            if (charge==1 && record.event.disposition!=StepDisposition::Applied) || (charge==0 && !matches!(record.event.disposition,StepDisposition::Published|StepDisposition::ExhaustedFuelUncharged)) {return Err(ProjectionGap::UnappliedSourceRule);}\n            self.completion=Some(PendingCompletion{line,charge,source_event:index});\n        }\n        let Some(completion)=&self.completion else {return Ok(ProjectionProgress::Pending{raw:record.clone()});};\n        let remaining=self.returned.remaining_fuel.checked_sub(completion.charge as u128).ok_or(ProjectionGap::ReferenceFuel)?;\n        let materialized=wp::materialize(&record.after).map_err(ProjectionGap::Witness)?;\n        let ReferenceBoundary::Complete{reference,..}=project_reference_boundary(&self.source,&record.after,&materialized.evaluation.decoded,self.initial.initial_fuel,remaining)? else {return Ok(ProjectionProgress::Pending{raw:record.clone()});};\n        let first=self.interval.first().ok_or(ProjectionGap::IncompleteInterval)?;\n        let first_materialized=wp::materialize(&first.before).map_err(ProjectionGap::Witness)?;\n        let ReferenceBoundary::Complete{reference:before,..}=project_reference_boundary(&self.source,&first.before,&first_materialized.evaluation.decoded,self.initial.initial_fuel,self.returned.remaining_fuel)? else {return Err(ProjectionGap::IncompleteInterval);};\n        if before!=self.returned{return Err(ProjectionGap::Discontinuity);}\n        let completed=a::StepRecord{rule_start_line:completion.line,charge:completion.charge,before,after:reference.clone()};\n        let span=ReferenceSpan{b_start:self.interval_start,b_end_exclusive:self.next_b,source_event:completion.source_event,raw:std::mem::take(&mut self.interval),reference:completed.clone()};\n        self.returned=reference;self.records.push(completed);self.completion=None;self.interval_start=self.next_b;\n        Ok(ProjectionProgress::Complete(span))\n    }\n    /// A trailing helper interval is retained and cannot masquerade as a full\n    /// reference prefix's returned boundary. Pending A calls at complete logical\n    /// boundaries are allowed; terminality is a separate observed property.\n    pub fn finish(&self)->Result<&a::Snapshot>{\n        if !self.interval.is_empty() || self.completion.is_some(){Err(ProjectionGap::IncompleteInterval)}else{Ok(&self.returned)}\n    }\n}\n\n=== END FULL BODY 03-full-consumed-projector ===\n\n=== BEGIN FULL BODY 04-full-A-types | /home/charl/Moriarty/.moriarty-dev/runtime/sherlock-review-20261017/witness-reference-projection-ordinary-QA-20261018/snapshot/crates/mori-core/src/sherlock/reference_types.rs | 5882 bytes | SHA256 4b4bb364a0c8182e117a9c36efb5d91cb7e405f653a6d3870f54dc03eefa317f ===\nuse std::collections::BTreeMap;\nuse std::sync::Arc;\n\npub const PROFILE: &str = \"sherlock-k-a/1\";\npub const K_SOURCE_SHA256: &str =\n    \"b3746ff51dd7999b046ccb23237595605420adcfeebc0c04c0ad0f1396b11d41\";\n\n/// Opaque source symbol. K comparisons use canonical signed-decimal names.\n/// Other spellings belong to the typed host API, outside that common domain.\npub type Name = String;\npub type Environment = BTreeMap<Name, Value>;\npub type ExprRef = Arc<Expr>;\n\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub enum Tree {\n    Leaf(u128),\n    Branch(Arc<Tree>, Arc<Tree>),\n}\n\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub enum Value {\n    UInt(u128),\n    Bool(bool),\n    List(Vec<u128>),\n    Tree(Tree),\n}\n\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub enum Type {\n    UInt,\n    Bool,\n    List,\n    Tree,\n}\n\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub enum BinaryOp {\n    Add,\n    Sub,\n    Mul,\n    Eq,\n    Lt,\n    Cons,\n    Branch,\n}\n\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub enum UnaryOp {\n    Leaf,\n    Not,\n}\n\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub enum Pattern {\n    Var(Name),\n    Nil,\n    Cons(Name, Name),\n    Leaf(Name),\n    Branch(Name, Name),\n}\n\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub struct Arm {\n    pub pattern: Pattern,\n    pub body: ExprRef,\n}\n\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub enum Expr {\n    Literal(Value),\n    Var(Name),\n    Let(Name, ExprRef, ExprRef),\n    Binary(BinaryOp, ExprRef, ExprRef),\n    Unary(UnaryOp, ExprRef),\n    If(ExprRef, ExprRef, ExprRef),\n    Call(Name, Vec<ExprRef>),\n    Match(ExprRef, Vec<Arm>),\n}\n\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub struct Parameter {\n    pub name: Name,\n    pub ty: Type,\n}\n\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub struct Function {\n    pub name: Name,\n    pub parameters: Vec<Parameter>,\n    pub return_type: Type,\n    pub body: ExprRef,\n}\n\n/// Function order is significant: lookup takes the first matching name.\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub struct Program {\n    pub functions: Vec<Function>,\n    pub entry: ExprRef,\n}\n\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub enum Frame {\n    Let(Name, ExprRef, Environment),\n    Left(BinaryOp, ExprRef, Environment),\n    Right(BinaryOp, Value),\n    Unary(UnaryOp),\n    If(ExprRef, ExprRef, Environment),\n    Match(Vec<Arm>, Environment),\n    Args(Name, Vec<Value>, Vec<ExprRef>, Environment),\n    Return(Type, Environment),\n    Scope(Environment),\n}\n\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub enum Control {\n    Eval(ExprRef),\n    Return(Value),\n    Push(Frame, Box<Control>, Environment),\n    Invoke(Name, Vec<Value>),\n    Enter(Option<Function>, Vec<Value>),\n    Bound(Option<Environment>, Type, ExprRef),\n    Cases(Value, Vec<Arm>, Environment),\n    CaseResult(Option<Environment>, Value, ExprRef, Vec<Arm>, Environment),\n    PrimitiveResult(Result<Value, u8>),\n    Error(u8),\n}\n\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub enum Outcome {\n    Pending,\n    Done(Value),\n    Rejected(u8),\n    Exhausted,\n}\n\nimpl Outcome {\n    /// Host-diagnostic classifier for the frozen `sherlock-k-a/1` A1 resource-limit partition.\n    ///\n    /// Returns `true` iff `self` is [`Outcome::Exhausted`] (zero-fuel termination) or\n    /// [`Outcome::Rejected(4)`] (K-A frame-cap overflow at `D >=Int L`). All other outcomes—\n    /// including [`Outcome::Pending`], [`Outcome::Done`], and all other [`Outcome::Rejected`]\n    /// codes (such as semantic, typing, binding, pattern, or arithmetic errors `3, 5..=11` and\n    /// unreachable literal code `2`)—return `false`.\n    ///\n    /// Scope: host diagnostic only on the `sherlock-k-a/1` typed common domain. This predicate\n    /// carries zero native or cryptographic authority, does not transfer across Quint\n    /// (`sherlock-quint-a/1`) or Candidate B (`sherlock-helper-microstep/1`), and does not make\n    /// the unmetered host evaluator safe for untrusted inputs. No consumer may interpret a\n    /// resource-limit outcome as a semantic, typing, or financial rejection.\n    pub const fn is_resource_limit(&self) -> bool {\n        matches!(self, Self::Exhausted | Self::Rejected(4))\n    }\n}\n\n/// Complete post-startup K boundary state on the typed host common domain.\n/// Frames are stored top first. `None` control represents K's `.K`.\n/// Snapshots are observations; no arbitrary-state import is exposed.\n///\n/// Machine invariant: every `Snapshot` produced by [`super::reference::Machine`] satisfies\n/// `remaining_fuel <= initial_fuel`.\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub struct Snapshot {\n    pub program: Arc<Program>,\n    pub control: Option<Control>,\n    pub environment: Environment,\n    pub frames: Vec<Frame>,\n    pub stack_limit: usize,\n    pub remaining_fuel: u128,\n    pub initial_fuel: u128,\n    pub outcome: Outcome,\n}\n\nimpl Snapshot {\n    pub fn depth(&self) -> usize {\n        self.frames.len()\n    }\n\n    /// Returns `initial_fuel - remaining_fuel` for machine-valid observations.\n    ///\n    /// # Preconditions\n    /// Requires the machine invariant `self.remaining_fuel <= self.initial_fuel`.\n    /// For hand-constructed snapshots where this invariant is not guaranteed, use\n    /// [`Snapshot::checked_charged_steps`] so invalid counters are reported as `None`\n    /// rather than silently clamped, wrapped, or panicked.\n    pub fn charged_steps(&self) -> u128 {\n        self.initial_fuel - self.remaining_fuel\n    }\n\n    /// Checked host-diagnostic step counter returning `None` if `remaining_fuel > initial_fuel`.\n    pub const fn checked_charged_steps(&self) -> Option<u128> {\n        self.initial_fuel.checked_sub(self.remaining_fuel)\n    }\n}\n\n/// A source rule transition, including free terminal publication.\n/// Line numbers refer only to `K_SOURCE_SHA256`, not to executed K rules.\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub struct StepRecord {\n    pub rule_start_line: usize,\n    pub charge: u8,\n    pub before: Snapshot,\n    pub after: Snapshot,\n}\n\n=== END FULL BODY 04-full-A-types ===\n\n=== BEGIN FULL BODY 05-full-actual-observation | /home/charl/Moriarty/.moriarty-dev/runtime/sherlock-review-20261017/witness-reference-projection-ordinary-QA-20261018/snapshot/crates/mori-core/src/sherlock/helper_machine/complete_observation.rs | 16561 bytes | SHA256 6b70d2ba8dc528fd6fcc5ca31d4e7f52e1a2115b853f2f55961462eae922ed5f ===\n//! Owned complete B host records around the existing fixed owner step.\n//!\n//! A diagnostic observer, not a new engine, guard, codec or transition validator.\n//! Every snapshot copies the actual owner-bound observation. Admission/source,\n//! native representation and source/transition authenticity are not established.\n//! Host allocation and copying costs are unmeasured and outside B work counters.\nuse super::raw::{ConstRow, DataRow};\nuse super::shared::*;\nuse super::shared::host_implied_prefix::SegBase;\nuse super::shared::owner_host::{host_owner_engine, observe_bound_image, HostObservation};\n\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub struct WidthsSnapshot {\n    pub index_widths: Vec<(String, u32)>,\n    pub counter_widths: Vec<(String, u32)>,\n    pub record_widths: Vec<(String, u32)>,\n}\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub struct LayoutSnapshot {\n    pub layout_version: (String, String),\n    pub field_id: Option<(String, String)>,\n    pub widths: Option<WidthsSnapshot>,\n    pub scalar_layout_id: Option<(String, String)>,\n    pub bounds: BoundsC,\n    pub capacities: LayoutCapacitiesC,\n    pub boundary_capacities_present: bool,\n}\n\n/// Same field/variant payloads as actual ExpressionRowC; no AST evaluation.\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub enum ExpressionSnapshot {\n    Literal { constant: usize },\n    Var { binder: usize },\n    Let { binder: usize, value: usize, body: usize },\n    Binary { op: BinaryOp, left: usize, right: usize },\n    Unary { op: UnaryOp, operand: usize },\n    If { cond: usize, then_expr: usize, else_expr: usize },\n    Call { function_name: usize, args: SliceC },\n    Match { scrutinee: usize, arms: SliceC },\n}\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub struct ConstFieldsSnapshot { pub start: usize, pub len: usize }\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub struct DataFieldsSnapshot { pub start: usize, pub len: usize }\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub enum ConstantSnapshot {\n    U128 { marker_free: bool, n: u128 },\n    Bool { marker_free: bool, b: bool },\n    Nil { marker_free: bool },\n    Cons { marker_free: bool, fields: ConstFieldsSnapshot },\n    Leaf { marker_free: bool, fields: ConstFieldsSnapshot },\n    Branch { marker_free: bool, fields: ConstFieldsSnapshot },\n    U128OutOfRange { marker_free: bool },\n}\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub enum DataSnapshot {\n    U128 { n: u128 },\n    Bool { b: bool },\n    Nil,\n    Cons { fields: DataFieldsSnapshot },\n    Leaf { fields: DataFieldsSnapshot },\n    Branch { fields: DataFieldsSnapshot },\n}\n\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub struct ProgramSnapshot {\n    pub entry: usize,\n    pub expressions: Vec<ExpressionSnapshot>,\n    pub occurrences: Vec<OccurrenceRowC>,\n    pub occurrence_paths: Vec<usize>,\n    pub children: Vec<usize>,\n    pub functions: Vec<FunctionRowC>,\n    pub parameters: Vec<ParameterRowC>,\n    pub arms: Vec<ArmRowC>,\n    pub patterns: Vec<PatternRowC>,\n    pub constants: Vec<ConstantSnapshot>,\n    pub constant_fields: Vec<usize>,\n    pub names: Vec<String>,\n}\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub struct AdmissionSnapshot {\n    pub identity: IdentityC,\n    pub bounds: BoundsC,\n    pub view: ProgramSnapshot,\n    pub layout: LayoutSnapshot,\n}\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub struct ImageSnapshot {\n    pub run_id: RunIdC,\n    pub control: ControlC,\n    pub control_origin: usize,\n    pub env_root: EnvRootC,\n    pub stack_limit: usize,\n    pub outcome: OutcomeC,\n    pub initial_fuel: u128,\n    pub remaining_work: u128,\n    pub consumed_work: u128,\n    pub helper_work: u128,\n    pub helper_visits: u128,\n    pub reference_cursor: u128,\n    pub alloc: AllocCounters,\n    pub active: ActiveLengths,\n    pub helper: Option<HelperControlC>,\n    pub result: Option<HelperResultC>,\n    pub seg_base: SegBase,\n    pub data: Vec<DataSnapshot>,\n    pub data_fields: Vec<RefC>,\n    pub env: Vec<EnvCellC>,\n    pub frames: Vec<FrameRowC>,\n    pub tasks: Vec<HelperTaskC>,\n    pub value_slots: Vec<RefC>,\n}\nimpl ImageSnapshot {\n    /// Derived exactly as the existing observation; no duplicate stored counter.\n    pub fn depth(&self) -> usize { self.frames.len() }\n    pub fn task_live(&self) -> usize { self.tasks.len() }\n}\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub struct HostSnapshot {\n    pub admission: AdmissionSnapshot,\n    pub image: ImageSnapshot,\n}\n\nfn expression(value: &ExpressionRowC) -> ExpressionSnapshot {\n    match value {\n        ExpressionRowC::Literal { constant } => ExpressionSnapshot::Literal { constant:*constant },\n        ExpressionRowC::Var { binder } => ExpressionSnapshot::Var { binder:*binder },\n        ExpressionRowC::Let { binder, value, body } => ExpressionSnapshot::Let { binder:*binder, value:*value, body:*body },\n        ExpressionRowC::Binary { op, left, right } => ExpressionSnapshot::Binary { op:*op, left:*left, right:*right },\n        ExpressionRowC::Unary { op, operand } => ExpressionSnapshot::Unary { op:*op, operand:*operand },\n        ExpressionRowC::If { cond, then_expr, else_expr } => ExpressionSnapshot::If { cond:*cond, then_expr:*then_expr, else_expr:*else_expr },\n        ExpressionRowC::Call { function_name, args } => ExpressionSnapshot::Call { function_name:*function_name, args:*args },\n        ExpressionRowC::Match { scrutinee, arms } => ExpressionSnapshot::Match { scrutinee:*scrutinee, arms:*arms },\n    }\n}\nfn constant(value: &ConstRow) -> ConstantSnapshot {\n    match value {\n        ConstRow::U128 { marker_free, n } => ConstantSnapshot::U128 { marker_free:*marker_free, n:*n },\n        ConstRow::Bool { marker_free, b } => ConstantSnapshot::Bool { marker_free:*marker_free, b:*b },\n        ConstRow::Nil { marker_free } => ConstantSnapshot::Nil { marker_free:*marker_free },\n        ConstRow::Cons { marker_free, fields } => ConstantSnapshot::Cons { marker_free:*marker_free,\n            fields:ConstFieldsSnapshot { start:fields.start.0, len:fields.len } },\n        ConstRow::Leaf { marker_free, fields } => ConstantSnapshot::Leaf { marker_free:*marker_free,\n            fields:ConstFieldsSnapshot { start:fields.start.0, len:fields.len } },\n        ConstRow::Branch { marker_free, fields } => ConstantSnapshot::Branch { marker_free:*marker_free,\n            fields:ConstFieldsSnapshot { start:fields.start.0, len:fields.len } },\n        ConstRow::U128OutOfRange { marker_free } => ConstantSnapshot::U128OutOfRange { marker_free:*marker_free },\n    }\n}\nfn data(value: &DataRow) -> DataSnapshot {\n    match value {\n        DataRow::U128 { n } => DataSnapshot::U128 { n:*n },\n        DataRow::Bool { b } => DataSnapshot::Bool { b:*b },\n        DataRow::Nil => DataSnapshot::Nil,\n        DataRow::Cons { fields } => DataSnapshot::Cons { fields:DataFieldsSnapshot { start:fields.start.0, len:fields.len } },\n        DataRow::Leaf { fields } => DataSnapshot::Leaf { fields:DataFieldsSnapshot { start:fields.start.0, len:fields.len } },\n        DataRow::Branch { fields } => DataSnapshot::Branch { fields:DataFieldsSnapshot { start:fields.start.0, len:fields.len } },\n    }\n}\n\n/// Copy every public field of the borrowed, bound host observation.\n/// Private zero-sized _sealed markers are construction markers, not observed data.\n/// Vec order/multiplicity, Option tags, raw references and marker_free remain exact.\npub fn copy_observation(value: HostObservation<'_>) -> HostSnapshot {\n    let admission = value.admission;\n    let layout = admission.layout;\n    let view = admission.view;\n    let image = value.image;\n    HostSnapshot {\n        admission:AdmissionSnapshot {\n            identity:(*admission.identity).clone(), bounds:*admission.bounds,\n            view:ProgramSnapshot {\n                entry:view.entry, expressions:view.expressions.iter().map(expression).collect(),\n                occurrences:view.occurrences.clone(), occurrence_paths:view.occurrence_paths.clone(),\n                children:view.children.clone(), functions:view.functions.clone(),\n                parameters:view.parameters.clone(), arms:view.arms.clone(), patterns:view.patterns.clone(),\n                constants:view.constants.iter().map(constant).collect(),\n                constant_fields:view.constant_fields.clone(), names:view.names.clone(),\n            },\n            layout:LayoutSnapshot {\n                layout_version:(*layout.layout_version).clone(), field_id:layout.field_id.cloned(),\n                widths:layout.widths.map(|widths| WidthsSnapshot {\n                    index_widths:widths.index_widths.to_vec(), counter_widths:widths.counter_widths.to_vec(),\n                    record_widths:widths.record_widths.to_vec(),\n                }),\n                scalar_layout_id:layout.scalar_layout_id.cloned(), bounds:*layout.bounds,\n                capacities:*layout.capacities, boundary_capacities_present:layout.boundary_capacities_present,\n            },\n        },\n        image:ImageSnapshot {\n            run_id:(*image.run_id).clone(), control:*image.control, control_origin:image.control_origin,\n            env_root:image.env_root, stack_limit:image.stack_limit, outcome:*image.outcome,\n            initial_fuel:image.initial_fuel, remaining_work:image.remaining_work,\n            consumed_work:image.consumed_work, helper_work:image.helper_work,\n            helper_visits:image.helper_visits, reference_cursor:image.reference_cursor,\n            alloc:*image.alloc, active:*image.active, helper:image.helper.copied(), result:image.result.copied(),\n            seg_base:image.seg_base, data:image.data.iter().map(data).collect(),\n            data_fields:image.data_fields.to_vec(), env:image.env.to_vec(), frames:image.frames.to_vec(),\n            tasks:image.tasks.to_vec(), value_slots:image.value_slots.to_vec(),\n        },\n    }\n}\n\npub fn capture(admitted: &Admitted, image: &MachineImage) -> Result<HostSnapshot, HostViolation> {\n    observe_bound_image(admitted, image).map(copy_observation)\n}\n\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub struct CompleteStepRecord {\n    pub before: HostSnapshot,\n    /// The actual complete owner event, including all counters/origins/locators.\n    pub event: StepEventC,\n    pub after: HostSnapshot,\n}\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub enum ObservedStep {\n    Event(CompleteStepRecord),\n    /// Actual Terminal result has no fabricated event or inferred mutation.\n    Terminal { before: HostSnapshot, after: HostSnapshot },\n}\npub enum CaptureStepError {\n    BeforeObservation(HostViolation),\n    /// The unchanged owner failure plus both available actual boundaries.\n    Step {\n        violation: HostViolation,\n        before: Box<HostSnapshot>,\n        after: Result<Box<HostSnapshot>, HostViolation>,\n    },\n    /// A real event/terminal disposition occurred, but no complete post record exists.\n    AfterObservation {\n        violation: HostViolation,\n        before: Box<HostSnapshot>,\n        event: Option<StepEventC>,\n    },\n}\n\n/// Capture owned pre-state before mutation, call the existing fixed owner once,\n/// then observe/copy actual post-state. This explicit stepping API consumes the\n/// caller's existing host-execution dependency; source integration does not admit it.\n/// No sink, expected data, new dispatcher, clock conversion or run loop is involved.\npub fn record_step(admitted: &Admitted, image: &mut MachineImage)\n    -> Result<ObservedStep, CaptureStepError>\n{\n    let before = capture(admitted, image).map_err(CaptureStepError::BeforeObservation)?;\n    let engine = host_owner_engine();\n    match engine.step(admitted, image) {\n        Ok(StepResult::Event { event }) => {\n            match capture(admitted, image) {\n                Ok(after) => Ok(ObservedStep::Event(CompleteStepRecord { before, event, after })),\n                Err(violation) => Err(CaptureStepError::AfterObservation {\n                    violation, before:Box::new(before), event:Some(event),\n                }),\n            }\n        }\n        Ok(StepResult::Terminal) => {\n            match capture(admitted, image) {\n                Ok(after) => Ok(ObservedStep::Terminal { before, after }),\n                Err(violation) => Err(CaptureStepError::AfterObservation {\n                    violation, before:Box::new(before), event:None,\n                }),\n            }\n        }\n        Err(violation) => Err(CaptureStepError::Step {\n            violation, before:Box::new(before), after:capture(admitted, image).map(Box::new),\n        }),\n    }\n}\n\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub enum ContinuityBoundary {\n    EmptyReturned,\n    InitialBefore,\n    Between { previous_record: usize, next_record: usize },\n    FinalReturned { final_record: usize },\n}\npub struct ContinuityDifference<'a> {\n    pub boundary: ContinuityBoundary,\n    pub expected: &'a HostSnapshot,\n    pub observed: &'a HostSnapshot,\n}\n\n/// Full typed boundary equality only. A match does not assert that events are\n/// valid, authenticate source, establish terminality or prove semantic refinement.\n/// A present empty sequence compares initial and returned state directly.\npub fn first_discontinuity<'a>(initial: &'a HostSnapshot,\n    records: &'a [CompleteStepRecord], returned: &'a HostSnapshot)\n    -> Option<ContinuityDifference<'a>>\n{\n    if records.is_empty() {\n        return (initial != returned).then_some(ContinuityDifference {\n            boundary:ContinuityBoundary::EmptyReturned, expected:initial, observed:returned,\n        });\n    }\n    if initial != &records[0].before {\n        return Some(ContinuityDifference {\n            boundary:ContinuityBoundary::InitialBefore, expected:initial, observed:&records[0].before,\n        });\n    }\n    for index in 1..records.len() {\n        if records[index - 1].after != records[index].before {\n            return Some(ContinuityDifference {\n                boundary:ContinuityBoundary::Between { previous_record:index - 1, next_record:index },\n                expected:&records[index - 1].after, observed:&records[index].before,\n            });\n        }\n    }\n    let final_record = records.len() - 1;\n    (&records[final_record].after != returned).then_some(ContinuityDifference {\n        boundary:ContinuityBoundary::FinalReturned { final_record },\n        expected:&records[final_record].after, observed:returned,\n    })\n}\n\n\n/// Optional witness materialization around the SAME existing fixed-owner step.\n/// The raw event/boundaries remain complete and unmodified. No run loop or\n/// transition evaluator is introduced. All plan/decode failures are tooling\n/// failures after the real step; raw boundaries survive and no retry is implied.\npub struct PlannedObservedStep {\n    pub observed: ObservedStep,\n    pub before: super::witness_plan::MaterializedSnapshot,\n    pub after: super::witness_plan::MaterializedSnapshot,\n}\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub enum WitnessSide { Before, After }\npub enum PlannedStepError {\n    Owner(CaptureStepError),\n    Materialization {\n        side: WitnessSide,\n        failure: super::witness_plan::WitnessFailure,\n        observed: Box<ObservedStep>,\n        completed_before: Option<Box<super::witness_plan::MaterializedSnapshot>>,\n    },\n}\n/// Execute existing record_step exactly once, then materialize its OWN saved\n/// boundaries. A tooling failure does not roll back or erase the actual step.\n/// Original capture/record_step signatures, raw semantics and owner errors stay\n/// unchanged. Cloning/decoding retains complete values; host costs remain H1 gaps.\npub fn record_step_with_plan(admitted: &Admitted, image: &mut MachineImage)\n    -> Result<PlannedObservedStep, PlannedStepError>\n{\n    use super::witness_plan::{materialize_for, LifetimeUnit};\n    let observed = record_step(admitted, image).map_err(PlannedStepError::Owner)?;\n    let (before_raw, after_raw) = match &observed {\n        ObservedStep::Event(record) => (&record.before, &record.after),\n        ObservedStep::Terminal { before, after } => (before, after),\n    };\n    let before = match materialize_for(before_raw, LifetimeUnit::RecordBefore) {\n        Ok(value) => value,\n        Err(failure) => return Err(PlannedStepError::Materialization {\n            side: WitnessSide::Before, failure, observed: Box::new(observed),\n            completed_before: None,\n        }),\n    };\n    let after = match materialize_for(after_raw, LifetimeUnit::RecordAfter) {\n        Ok(value) => value,\n        Err(failure) => return Err(PlannedStepError::Materialization {\n            side: WitnessSide::After, failure, observed: Box::new(observed),\n            completed_before: Some(Box::new(before)),\n        }),\n    };\n    Ok(PlannedObservedStep { observed, before, after })\n}\n\n=== END FULL BODY 05-full-actual-observation ===\n\n=== BEGIN FULL BODY 06-full-witness-types-api | /home/charl/Moriarty/.moriarty-dev/runtime/sherlock-review-20261017/witness-reference-projection-ordinary-QA-20261018/snapshot/crates/mori-core/src/sherlock/helper_machine/witness_plan.rs | 12255 bytes | SHA256 069c78ce06e093409a038ae3e9b36d2fa76585f843aa9f733e128461a96932a9 ===\n//! Deterministic host materialization of existing B observations.\n//!\n//! This read-only plan does not evaluate source expressions, select owner rules,\n//! modify an image, emit constraints or authenticate supplied snapshots. Plans\n//! bind exact immutable observation inputs. Existing uncached entrypoints execute\n//! every node once per call. Optional memoization and last-use/streaming APIs\n//! retain the same operations and complete raw/decoded boundaries, with separate\n//! logical host diagnostics. Physical allocation/copy/time costs and H1 remain\n//! unmeasured; no native, resource, A/B-clock or correspondence claim is made.\nuse super::complete_observation::{\n    AdmissionSnapshot, ConstantSnapshot, DataSnapshot, ExpressionSnapshot, HostSnapshot,\n};\nuse super::shared::*;\nuse super::shared::host_implied_prefix::SegBase;\n\n#[path = \"witness_plan/dag.rs\"]\nmod dag;\n#[path = \"witness_plan/decode.rs\"]\nmod decode;\n\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, PartialOrd, Ord)]\npub struct NodeId(pub usize);\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, PartialOrd, Ord)]\npub struct BindingId(pub usize);\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub enum LifetimeUnit { Snapshot, RecordBefore, RecordAfter }\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub struct Location {\n    pub section: &'static str,\n    pub row: Option<usize>,\n    pub field: &'static str,\n}\nimpl Location {\n    pub fn new(section: &'static str, row: Option<usize>, field: &'static str) -> Self {\n        Self { section, row, field }\n    }\n}\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub enum FailureKind {\n    MissingInput, InputChanged, IndexOverflow, CyclicValue, CyclicEnvironment,\n    WrongArity { expected: usize, actual: usize },\n    WrongValueSort { expected: SortTag, actual: Option<SortTag> },\n    MissingDependency { dependency: NodeId },\n    WrongType { expected: ValueType, actual: ValueType },\n    InvalidNodeId, CyclicDependencies, UnstableOrder, IncompleteBindings,\n    IncompleteOutputs, WrongOperation,\n}\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub struct WitnessFailure {\n    pub location: Location,\n    pub node: Option<NodeId>,\n    pub kind: FailureKind,\n}\npub(super) fn fail(location: Location, kind: FailureKind) -> WitnessFailure {\n    WitnessFailure { location, node: None, kind }\n}\n\n/// One flat, fully unfolded occurrence tree. Child indices precede parents;\n/// repeated raw references produce repeated semantic occurrences, not sharing.\n/// Vec ownership avoids recursive construction, traversal and recursive Drop.\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub enum ValueNode {\n    UInt(u128), Bool(bool), Nil, U128OutOfRange,\n    Cons { head: usize, tail: usize }, Leaf { value: usize },\n    Branch { left: usize, right: usize },\n}\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub struct DecodedValue { pub nodes: Vec<ValueNode>, pub root: usize }\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub struct EnvironmentEntry {\n    pub binder: usize,\n    pub name: String,\n    pub value: DecodedValue,\n}\n/// Exact newest-to-oldest chain, retaining duplicate binders and shadowed cells.\n/// An empty successful binding remains distinct from a failed BoundBinding.\npub type DecodedEnvironment = Vec<EnvironmentEntry>;\n\n/// Full non-table image fields; tables have explicit separate output bindings.\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub struct Metadata {\n    pub admission: AdmissionSnapshot,\n    pub run_id: RunIdC,\n    pub control_origin: usize,\n    pub env_root: EnvRootC,\n    pub stack_limit: usize,\n    pub initial_fuel: u128,\n    pub remaining_work: u128,\n    pub consumed_work: u128,\n    pub helper_work: u128,\n    pub helper_visits: u128,\n    pub reference_cursor: u128,\n    pub alloc: AllocCounters,\n    pub active: ActiveLengths,\n    pub seg_base: SegBase,\n    /// data/data_fields/env/frames/tasks/value_slots, in that order.\n    pub table_lengths: [usize; 6],\n}\n\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, PartialOrd, Ord)]\npub enum InputPath {\n    Metadata, Constant(usize), ConstantField(usize), Data(usize), DataField(usize),\n    Environment(usize), Name(usize), Expression(usize), Function(usize),\n    Parameter(usize), Arm(usize), Pattern(usize), Occurrence(usize),\n    OccurrencePath(usize), Child(usize), Frame(usize), ScheduledFrame,\n    Control, Helper, Task(usize), Result, Outcome, ValueSlot(usize),\n}\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub enum SourceType {\n    Metadata, Constant, Data, Reference, Environment, Name, Expression, Function,\n    Parameter, Arm, Pattern, Occurrence, Index, Frame, Control, Helper, Task,\n    Result, Outcome,\n}\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub enum InputValue {\n    Metadata(Metadata), Constant(ConstantSnapshot), Data(DataSnapshot),\n    Reference(RefC), Environment(EnvCellC), Name(String),\n    Expression(ExpressionSnapshot), Function(FunctionRowC), Parameter(ParameterRowC),\n    Arm(ArmRowC), Pattern(PatternRowC), Occurrence(OccurrenceRowC), Index(usize),\n    Frame(FrameRowC), Control(ControlC), Helper(Option<HelperControlC>),\n    Task(HelperTaskC), Result(Option<HelperResultC>), Outcome(OutcomeC),\n}\nimpl InputValue {\n    pub fn source_type(&self) -> SourceType {\n        match self {\n            Self::Metadata(_) => SourceType::Metadata, Self::Constant(_) => SourceType::Constant,\n            Self::Data(_) => SourceType::Data, Self::Reference(_) => SourceType::Reference,\n            Self::Environment(_) => SourceType::Environment, Self::Name(_) => SourceType::Name,\n            Self::Expression(_) => SourceType::Expression, Self::Function(_) => SourceType::Function,\n            Self::Parameter(_) => SourceType::Parameter, Self::Arm(_) => SourceType::Arm,\n            Self::Pattern(_) => SourceType::Pattern, Self::Occurrence(_) => SourceType::Occurrence,\n            Self::Index(_) => SourceType::Index, Self::Frame(_) => SourceType::Frame,\n            Self::Control(_) => SourceType::Control, Self::Helper(_) => SourceType::Helper,\n            Self::Task(_) => SourceType::Task, Self::Result(_) => SourceType::Result,\n            Self::Outcome(_) => SourceType::Outcome,\n        }\n    }\n}\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub enum PayloadKind { Frame, Control, Helper, Task, Result, Outcome }\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub enum SequenceKind { Values, Environments, Frames, Tasks, Names, Expressions, Parameters, Arms, Patterns, Occurrences, Indices, References }\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub enum ValueType {\n    Source(SourceType), Value, Environment, Payload(PayloadKind),\n    Sequence(SequenceKind), Snapshot,\n}\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub struct NamedValue { pub field: &'static str, pub value: SlotValue }\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub struct DecodedPayload {\n    pub kind: PayloadKind,\n    /// Exact tag and all scalar/cursor/origin/status fields, never normalized.\n    pub raw: InputValue,\n    pub fields: Vec<NamedValue>,\n}\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub struct DecodedSnapshot { pub metadata: Metadata, pub fields: Vec<NamedValue> }\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub enum SlotValue {\n    Source(InputValue), Value(DecodedValue), Environment(DecodedEnvironment),\n    Payload(DecodedPayload), Sequence { kind: SequenceKind, items: Vec<SlotValue> },\n    Snapshot(DecodedSnapshot),\n}\nimpl SlotValue {\n    pub fn value_type(&self) -> ValueType {\n        match self {\n            Self::Source(value) => ValueType::Source(value.source_type()),\n            Self::Value(_) => ValueType::Value, Self::Environment(_) => ValueType::Environment,\n            Self::Payload(value) => ValueType::Payload(value.kind),\n            Self::Sequence { kind, .. } => ValueType::Sequence(*kind), Self::Snapshot(_) => ValueType::Snapshot,\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub struct InputBinding {\n    pub id: BindingId,\n    pub path: InputPath,\n    pub value_type: SourceType,\n    pub immutable_value: InputValue,\n    pub location: Location,\n}\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub struct Dependency { pub node: NodeId, pub value_type: ValueType }\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub struct FieldBinding { pub field: &'static str, pub dependency: Dependency }\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub enum Operation {\n    Read(BindingId),\n    /// A raw member/reference and its resolved target, in that order.\n    Bind,\n    /// Row, then ordered (field-reference, decoded-child) pairs.\n    Value { source: RefC, arity: usize },\n    EmptyEnvironment,\n    /// Environment-cell, name, decoded-value, previous-environment.\n    Environment,\n    Sequence { kind: SequenceKind, item_type: ValueType },\n    /// First dependency is the exact raw payload; fields are remaining inputs.\n    Payload { kind: PayloadKind, fields: Vec<FieldBinding> },\n    /// First dependency is metadata; every remaining output is named explicitly.\n    Snapshot { fields: Vec<FieldBinding> },\n}\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub struct Node {\n    pub id: NodeId,\n    pub location: Location,\n    pub operation: Operation,\n    pub dependencies: Vec<Dependency>,\n    pub output_type: ValueType,\n}\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub struct Definition {\n    pub value: NodeId,\n    pub producer: NodeId,\n    /// Ordered consumer edges, including repeated uses within one consumer.\n    pub consumers: Vec<NodeId>,\n    pub last_use_order: usize,\n    pub lifetime: LifetimeUnit,\n    pub live_out: bool,\n}\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub struct WitnessPlan {\n    pub format: &'static str,\n    pub lifetime: LifetimeUnit,\n    pub inputs: Vec<InputBinding>,\n    pub nodes: Vec<Node>,\n    pub stable_topological_order: Vec<NodeId>,\n    pub definitions: Vec<Definition>,\n    pub live_outs: Vec<NodeId>,\n    pub output: NodeId,\n}\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Default)]\npub struct HostDiagnostics {\n    pub evaluated_nodes: usize,\n    pub input_reads: usize,\n    pub value_constructions: usize,\n    pub environment_constructions: usize,\n    pub payload_constructions: usize,\n    /// Only child nodes copied within Value operations, not all host clones.\n    pub copied_value_nodes: usize,\n    /// Only prior-chain entries copied within Environment operations.\n    pub copied_environment_entries: usize,\n    /// Scratch slots at publication: all nodes in the uncached baseline,\n    /// potentially fewer after last-use. Not allocated bytes/prover memory.\n    pub retained_slots: usize,\n    pub measured_host_bytes: Option<usize>,\n    pub measured_host_time_ns: Option<u128>,\n}\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub struct WitnessEvaluation {\n    pub decoded: DecodedSnapshot,\n    pub diagnostics: HostDiagnostics,\n}\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub struct MaterializedSnapshot {\n    pub raw: HostSnapshot,\n    pub plan: WitnessPlan,\n    pub evaluation: WitnessEvaluation,\n}\n\npub fn construct_plan(input: &HostSnapshot) -> Result<WitnessPlan, WitnessFailure> {\n    construct_plan_for(input, LifetimeUnit::Snapshot)\n}\npub fn construct_plan_for(input: &HostSnapshot, lifetime: LifetimeUnit)\n    -> Result<WitnessPlan, WitnessFailure>\n{\n    decode::build(input, lifetime)\n}\npub fn evaluate_uncached(plan: &WitnessPlan, input: &HostSnapshot)\n    -> Result<WitnessEvaluation, WitnessFailure>\n{\n    dag::evaluate(plan, input)\n}\npub fn materialize(input: &HostSnapshot) -> Result<MaterializedSnapshot, WitnessFailure> {\n    materialize_for(input, LifetimeUnit::Snapshot)\n}\npub fn materialize_for(input: &HostSnapshot, lifetime: LifetimeUnit)\n    -> Result<MaterializedSnapshot, WitnessFailure>\n{\n    let plan = construct_plan_for(input, lifetime)?;\n    let evaluation = evaluate_uncached(&plan, input)?;\n    Ok(MaterializedSnapshot { raw: input.clone(), plan, evaluation })\n}\n\n// Optional host scheduling strategies reuse the same validated DAG operations.\n#[path = \"witness_plan/strategy.rs\"]\nmod strategy;\npub use strategy::{\n    evaluate_last_use, evaluate_memoized, evaluate_with_storage,\n    SlotStorage, StrategyDiagnostics, StrategyEvaluation, WitnessCache,\n};\n#[path = \"witness_plan/stream.rs\"]\nmod stream;\npub use stream::{\n    materialize_with_storage, record_step_with_storage, stream_owner_steps,\n    StrategyMaterializedSnapshot, StrategyObservedStep, StrategyStepError,\n    WitnessRecordCache, StreamAction, StreamStop,\n};\n\n=== END FULL BODY 06-full-witness-types-api ===\n\n=== BEGIN FULL BODY 07-full-cache-strategy | /home/charl/Moriarty/.moriarty-dev/runtime/sherlock-review-20261017/witness-reference-projection-ordinary-QA-20261018/snapshot/crates/mori-core/src/sherlock/helper_machine/witness_plan/strategy.rs | 8718 bytes | SHA256 d437ba618b74303bd4fb01f2a1292d69b0f9e3148dc54466f821c6b4d7ba5cb4 ===\n//! Optional memoization and scratch-slot lifetimes for the existing witness DAG.\n//!\n//! This executes only `dag::operation`, never B/source transitions. Exact typed\n//! keys use full equality, not hashes: program/profile/layout/admission, graph,\n//! binding paths/types, and each operation's complete immutable argument values.\n//! Every Read and the unchanged plan validation still execute on warm calls.\n//! A cache retains one graph, with one most-recent argument/result entry per\n//! non-Read node. There is no global cache, eviction budget or admission policy.\n//! Logical slots/operations below are not measured bytes, allocator traffic,\n//! total clones, elapsed time, B work, or a physical-memory improvement claim.\nuse super::*;\n\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub enum SlotStorage { RetainAll, LastUse }\n\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Default)]\npub struct StrategyDiagnostics {\n    /// Every node in the original stable order, including memo hits.\n    pub scheduled_nodes: usize,\n    pub cache_hits: usize,\n    /// Only non-Read misses; all Read nodes always execute separately.\n    pub cache_misses: usize,\n    pub scope_reset: bool,\n    /// Values cloned out of memo entries, excluding key/argument/other clones.\n    pub copied_cached_slot_values: usize,\n    pub reclaimed_slots: usize,\n    /// Scratch slots only; excludes retained raw records, plan, sink and cache.\n    pub peak_live_slots: usize,\n    pub retained_slots_at_publication: usize,\n    pub cached_value_slots: usize,\n    /// Top-level argument cells retained as exact keys, not recursive bytes.\n    pub cached_argument_slots: usize,\n}\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub struct StrategyEvaluation {\n    /// Complete decoded output; HostDiagnostics counts only executed operations.\n    /// `retained_slots` is the scratch count immediately before publication.\n    pub witness: WitnessEvaluation,\n    pub scheduling: StrategyDiagnostics,\n}\n\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\nstruct BindingShape {\n    id: BindingId,\n    path: InputPath,\n    value_type: SourceType,\n    location: Location,\n}\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\nstruct CacheScope {\n    format: &'static str,\n    lifetime: LifetimeUnit,\n    admission: AdmissionSnapshot,\n    nodes: Vec<Node>,\n    bindings: Vec<BindingShape>,\n}\nimpl CacheScope {\n    fn new(plan: &WitnessPlan, input: &HostSnapshot) -> Self {\n        Self {\n            format: plan.format, lifetime: plan.lifetime,\n            admission: input.admission.clone(), nodes: plan.nodes.clone(),\n            bindings: plan.inputs.iter().map(|b| BindingShape {\n                id: b.id, path: b.path, value_type: b.value_type, location: b.location,\n            }).collect(),\n        }\n    }\n}\nstruct MemoEntry {\n    /// Full values preserve all raw tags, ordered multiplicity and occurrences.\n    arguments: Vec<SlotValue>,\n    value: SlotValue,\n}\n#[derive(Default)]\npub struct WitnessCache {\n    scope: Option<CacheScope>,\n    entries: Vec<Option<MemoEntry>>,\n}\nimpl WitnessCache {\n    pub fn clear(&mut self) { self.scope = None; self.entries.clear(); }\n    pub fn value_slots(&self) -> usize {\n        self.entries.iter().filter(|entry| entry.is_some()).count()\n    }\n    pub fn argument_slots(&self) -> usize {\n        self.entries.iter().filter_map(Option::as_ref).map(|e| e.arguments.len()).sum()\n    }\n    fn bind(&mut self, plan: &WitnessPlan, input: &HostSnapshot) -> bool {\n        let scope = CacheScope::new(plan, input);\n        if self.scope.as_ref() == Some(&scope) { return false; }\n        self.scope = Some(scope);\n        self.entries = (0..plan.nodes.len()).map(|_| None).collect();\n        true\n    }\n}\n\npub fn evaluate_last_use(plan: &WitnessPlan, input: &HostSnapshot)\n    -> Result<StrategyEvaluation, WitnessFailure>\n{\n    evaluate_with_storage(plan, input, SlotStorage::LastUse, None)\n}\npub fn evaluate_memoized(plan: &WitnessPlan, input: &HostSnapshot,\n    cache: &mut WitnessCache, storage: SlotStorage)\n    -> Result<StrategyEvaluation, WitnessFailure>\n{\n    evaluate_with_storage(plan, input, storage, Some(cache))\n}\n\n/// Preserve the baseline's complete validation, order and operation semantics.\n/// Last-use only releases scratch values after their final ordered consumer;\n/// boundary live-outs remain through publication. Cached copies are accounted\n/// separately and are not reported as reclaimed scratch or semantic savings.\npub fn evaluate_with_storage(plan: &WitnessPlan, input: &HostSnapshot,\n    storage: SlotStorage, mut cache: Option<&mut WitnessCache>)\n    -> Result<StrategyEvaluation, WitnessFailure>\n{\n    let at = Location::new(\"plan\", None, \"structure\");\n    let schedule = dag::validate(plan)?;\n    let mut scheduling = StrategyDiagnostics::default();\n    if let Some(memo) = cache.as_deref_mut() {\n        scheduling.scope_reset = memo.bind(plan, input);\n    }\n    let mut release = vec![Vec::new(); schedule.len()];\n    if storage == SlotStorage::LastUse {\n        for definition in &plan.definitions {\n            // validate() compared these exact definitions to the existing\n            // recomputation; every non-live-out last-use is a schedule position.\n            if !definition.live_out {\n                release[definition.last_use_order].push(definition.value);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    let mut slots: Vec<Option<SlotValue>> = vec![None; plan.nodes.len()];\n    let mut diagnostics = HostDiagnostics::default();\n    let mut live = 0;\n    for (position, id) in schedule.into_iter().enumerate() {\n        let node = &plan.nodes[id.0];\n        let result = {\n            let mut args = Vec::new();\n            for dependency in &node.dependencies {\n                let value = slots.get(dependency.node.0).and_then(Option::as_ref)\n                    .ok_or_else(|| dag::node_failure(node, FailureKind::MissingDependency {\n                        dependency: dependency.node,\n                    }))?;\n                if value.value_type() != dependency.value_type {\n                    return Err(dag::node_failure(node, FailureKind::WrongType {\n                        expected: dependency.value_type, actual: value.value_type(),\n                    }));\n                }\n                args.push(value);\n            }\n            // Reads are never bypassed: InputChanged/type/location behavior is\n            // the existing operation's behavior, including warm evaluations.\n            let memoizable = !matches!(node.operation, Operation::Read(_));\n            let cached = if memoizable {\n                cache.as_deref().and_then(|memo| memo.entries[id.0].as_ref())\n                    .filter(|entry| entry.arguments.len() == args.len()\n                        && entry.arguments.iter().zip(&args).all(|(a, b)| a == *b))\n            } else { None };\n            if let Some(entry) = cached {\n                scheduling.cache_hits += 1;\n                scheduling.copied_cached_slot_values += 1;\n                entry.value.clone()\n            } else {\n                let value = dag::operation(plan, input, node, &args, &mut diagnostics)?;\n                diagnostics.evaluated_nodes += 1;\n                if memoizable {\n                    if let Some(memo) = cache.as_deref_mut() {\n                        scheduling.cache_misses += 1;\n                        memo.entries[id.0] = Some(MemoEntry {\n                            arguments: args.iter().map(|value| (**value).clone()).collect(),\n                            value: value.clone(),\n                        });\n                    }\n                }\n                value\n            }\n        };\n        if result.value_type() != node.output_type {\n            return Err(dag::node_failure(node, FailureKind::WrongType {\n                expected: node.output_type, actual: result.value_type(),\n            }));\n        }\n        slots[id.0] = Some(result);\n        live += 1;\n        scheduling.scheduled_nodes += 1;\n        scheduling.peak_live_slots = scheduling.peak_live_slots.max(live);\n        for dead in &release[position] {\n            if slots[dead.0].take().is_some() {\n                live -= 1;\n                scheduling.reclaimed_slots += 1;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    diagnostics.retained_slots = live;\n    scheduling.retained_slots_at_publication = live;\n    if let Some(memo) = cache.as_deref() {\n        scheduling.cached_value_slots = memo.value_slots();\n        scheduling.cached_argument_slots = memo.argument_slots();\n    }\n    let Some(SlotValue::Snapshot(decoded)) = slots.get_mut(plan.output.0).and_then(Option::take) else {\n        return Err(fail(at, FailureKind::IncompleteOutputs));\n    };\n    Ok(StrategyEvaluation {\n        witness: WitnessEvaluation { decoded, diagnostics }, scheduling,\n    })\n}\n\n=== END FULL BODY 07-full-cache-strategy ===\n\n=== BEGIN FULL BODY 08-full-owner-stream-consumer | /home/charl/Moriarty/.moriarty-dev/runtime/sherlock-review-20261017/witness-reference-projection-ordinary-QA-20261018/snapshot/crates/mori-core/src/sherlock/helper_machine/witness_plan/stream.rs | 5014 bytes | SHA256 21b1ecd3d8db3f2913d5829831892d4102540436a2da5fc703b067f76d26bad6 ===\n//! Complete record streaming around the SAME fixed-owner observation interface.\n//!\n//! The library retains no record history. The callback sees a complete borrowed\n//! record, then its raw/materialized buffers are dropped before the next step.\n//! A retaining caller/sink can still retain everything; no measured memory/time\n//! improvement or semantic-prefix/clock theorem is implied by this interface.\nuse super::{\n    construct_plan_for, evaluate_with_storage, HostSnapshot, LifetimeUnit,\n    SlotStorage, StrategyEvaluation, WitnessCache, WitnessFailure, WitnessPlan,\n};\nuse crate::sherlock::helper_machine::complete_observation::{\n    self as observation, CaptureStepError, ObservedStep, WitnessSide,\n};\nuse crate::sherlock::helper_machine::shared::{Admitted, MachineImage};\n\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub struct StrategyMaterializedSnapshot {\n    pub raw: HostSnapshot,\n    pub plan: WitnessPlan,\n    pub evaluation: StrategyEvaluation,\n}\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub struct StrategyObservedStep {\n    pub observed: ObservedStep,\n    pub before: StrategyMaterializedSnapshot,\n    pub after: StrategyMaterializedSnapshot,\n}\npub enum StrategyStepError {\n    Owner(CaptureStepError),\n    Materialization {\n        side: WitnessSide,\n        failure: WitnessFailure,\n        observed: Box<ObservedStep>,\n        completed_before: Option<Box<StrategyMaterializedSnapshot>>,\n    },\n}\n/// Separate before/after lifetime namespaces retain one graph each, not history.\n#[derive(Default)]\npub struct WitnessRecordCache { before: WitnessCache, after: WitnessCache }\nimpl WitnessRecordCache {\n    pub fn clear(&mut self) { self.before.clear(); self.after.clear(); }\n}\n\npub fn materialize_with_storage(input: &HostSnapshot, lifetime: LifetimeUnit,\n    storage: SlotStorage, cache: Option<&mut WitnessCache>)\n    -> Result<StrategyMaterializedSnapshot, WitnessFailure>\n{\n    let plan = construct_plan_for(input, lifetime)?;\n    let evaluation = evaluate_with_storage(&plan, input, storage, cache)?;\n    Ok(StrategyMaterializedSnapshot { raw: input.clone(), plan, evaluation })\n}\n\n/// One real owner step, followed solely by reconstruction of its saved raw\n/// boundaries. On any tooling failure, the actual step and available boundaries\n/// are returned unchanged; no rollback, retry or extra transition is performed.\npub fn record_step_with_storage(admitted: &Admitted, image: &mut MachineImage,\n    storage: SlotStorage, mut cache: Option<&mut WitnessRecordCache>)\n    -> Result<StrategyObservedStep, StrategyStepError>\n{\n    let observed = observation::record_step(admitted, image).map_err(StrategyStepError::Owner)?;\n    let (before_raw, after_raw) = match &observed {\n        ObservedStep::Event(record) => (&record.before, &record.after),\n        ObservedStep::Terminal { before, after } => (before, after),\n    };\n    let before_cache = cache.as_deref_mut().map(|memo| &mut memo.before);\n    let before = match materialize_with_storage(before_raw, LifetimeUnit::RecordBefore, storage, before_cache) {\n        Ok(value) => value,\n        Err(failure) => return Err(StrategyStepError::Materialization {\n            side: WitnessSide::Before, failure, observed: Box::new(observed),\n            completed_before: None,\n        }),\n    };\n    let after_cache = cache.as_deref_mut().map(|memo| &mut memo.after);\n    let after = match materialize_with_storage(after_raw, LifetimeUnit::RecordAfter, storage, after_cache) {\n        Ok(value) => value,\n        Err(failure) => return Err(StrategyStepError::Materialization {\n            side: WitnessSide::After, failure, observed: Box::new(observed),\n            completed_before: Some(Box::new(before)),\n        }),\n    };\n    Ok(StrategyObservedStep { observed, before, after })\n}\n\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub enum StreamAction { Continue, Stop }\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub enum StreamStop { Sink, Terminal }\n\n/// Yield every complete observed record/terminal boundary in order. The sink\n/// may stop after a delivered boundary, preserving that exact caller-owned\n/// MachineImage. No inferred work/event, hidden step, image substitution or\n/// application exhaustion is introduced. Execution classification remains the\n/// existing caller's obligation, independently of this source-only interface.\npub fn stream_owner_steps<F>(admitted: &Admitted, image: &mut MachineImage,\n    mut cache: Option<&mut WitnessRecordCache>, mut sink: F)\n    -> Result<StreamStop, StrategyStepError>\nwhere F: FnMut(&StrategyObservedStep) -> StreamAction\n{\n    loop {\n        let step = record_step_with_storage(admitted, image, SlotStorage::LastUse, cache.as_deref_mut())?;\n        let terminal = matches!(&step.observed, ObservedStep::Terminal { .. });\n        let action = sink(&step);\n        // No decoded/raw record history is held across loop iterations.\n        drop(step);\n        if terminal { return Ok(StreamStop::Terminal); }\n        if action == StreamAction::Stop { return Ok(StreamStop::Sink); }\n    }\n}\n\n=== END FULL BODY 08-full-owner-stream-consumer ===\n\n=== BEGIN FULL BODY 09-exact-three-operations | /home/charl/Moriarty/.moriarty-dev/runtime/sherlock-review-20261017/witness-reference-contrast-source-20261018/revision02-B0-schedule/ordinary-QA/PROPOSED.json | 10273 bytes | SHA256 4f019e4c5ade0e798a4b981c823677045490ce2979c7befb737a9f2eabcfb091 ===\n{\n  \"status\": \"PREPARED_UNRUN_ADDITIVE_B0_FRESH_REVIEW_ROOT_SELECTION_PENDING\",\n  \"operations\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"01-compileWitnessReferenceCountercaseConsumer\",\n      \"argv\": [\n        \"/usr/bin/timeout\",\n        \"--signal=KILL\",\n        \"30s\",\n        \"/usr/bin/prlimit\",\n        \"--cpu=25:25\",\n        \"--as=2147483648:2147483648\",\n        \"--fsize=67108864:67108864\",\n        \"--core=0:0\",\n        \"--\",\n        \"/home/charl/.rustup/toolchains/1.99.0-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/bin/rustc\",\n        \"--sysroot\",\n        \"/home/charl/.rustup/toolchains/1.99.0-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu\",\n        \"--target\",\n        \"x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu\",\n        \"--edition=2024\",\n        \"--crate-name\",\n        \"witness_reference_contrast_positive\",\n        \"--test\",\n        \"/home/charl/Moriarty/.moriarty-dev/runtime/sherlock-review-20261017/witness-reference-contrast-source-20261018/revision02-B0-schedule/afterimages/crates/mori-core/tests/support/sherlock_witness_reference_contrast_positive.rs\",\n        \"--extern\",\n        \"mori_core=/home/charl/Moriarty/.moriarty-dev/runtime/sherlock-review-20261017/witness-reference-projection-ordinary-QA-20261018/build/libmori_core.rlib\",\n        \"--extern\",\n        \"serde_json=/home/charl/Moriarty/.moriarty-dev/runtime/sherlock-review-20261017/24-compiler-qa/proposed-run/core-target/debug/deps/libserde_json-76dc87088753b61e.rlib\",\n        \"-L\",\n        \"dependency=/home/charl/Moriarty/.moriarty-dev/runtime/sherlock-review-20261017/witness-reference-projection-ordinary-QA-20261018/build\",\n        \"-L\",\n        \"dependency=/home/charl/Moriarty/.moriarty-dev/runtime/sherlock-review-20261017/191-bounded-parser-ordinary-qa/build\",\n        \"-L\",\n        \"dependency=/home/charl/Moriarty/.moriarty-dev/runtime/sherlock-review-20261017/24-compiler-qa/proposed-run/core-target/debug/deps\",\n        \"--emit=link,dep-info=/home/charl/Moriarty/.moriarty-dev/runtime/sherlock-review-20261017/witness-reference-contrast-source-20261018/revision02-B0-schedule/ordinary-QA/build/witness-reference-contrast-positive.d\",\n        \"-o\",\n        \"/home/charl/Moriarty/.moriarty-dev/runtime/sherlock-review-20261017/witness-reference-contrast-source-20261018/revision02-B0-schedule/ordinary-QA/build/witness-reference-contrast-positive\",\n        \"-C\",\n        \"debuginfo=0\",\n        \"-C\",\n        \"opt-level=0\",\n        \"-C\",\n        \"debug-assertions=yes\",\n        \"-C\",\n        \"linker=/usr/bin/x86_64-linux-gnu-gcc-15\",\n        \"-C\",\n        \"link-arg=-fuse-ld=bfd\"\n      ],\n      \"cwd\": \"/home/charl/Moriarty/.moriarty-dev/runtime/sherlock-review-20261017/witness-reference-contrast-source-20261018/revision02-B0-schedule/ordinary-QA\",\n      \"environment\": {\n        \"PATH\": \"/usr/bin:/bin\",\n        \"LANG\": \"C.UTF-8\",\n        \"TMPDIR\": \"/home/charl/Moriarty/.moriarty-dev/runtime/sherlock-review-20261017/witness-reference-contrast-source-20261018/revision02-B0-schedule/ordinary-QA/tmp\"\n      },\n      \"outputs\": [\n        \"/home/charl/Moriarty/.moriarty-dev/runtime/sherlock-review-20261017/witness-reference-contrast-source-20261018/revision02-B0-schedule/ordinary-QA/build/witness-reference-contrast-positive\",\n        \"/home/charl/Moriarty/.moriarty-dev/runtime/sherlock-review-20261017/witness-reference-contrast-source-20261018/revision02-B0-schedule/ordinary-QA/build/witness-reference-contrast-positive.d\"\n      ],\n      \"status\": \"PROPOSED_UNRUN_FRESH_FULL_REVISED_SOURCE_AND_OPERATION_REVIEW_REQUIRED\",\n      \"wallSeconds\": 30,\n      \"keptBytesPerStream\": 131072,\n      \"environmentPolicy\": \"Exactly declared vars; no inherited environment\",\n      \"serialFailStopNoRetry\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"02-factorial_two_complete_prefix_program_cache_and_incomplete_stream\",\n      \"argv\": [\n        \"/usr/bin/timeout\",\n        \"--signal=KILL\",\n        \"10s\",\n        \"/usr/bin/prlimit\",\n        \"--cpu=8:8\",\n        \"--as=1073741824:1073741824\",\n        \"--fsize=16777216:16777216\",\n        \"--core=0:0\",\n        \"--\",\n        \"/home/charl/Moriarty/.moriarty-dev/runtime/sherlock-review-20261017/witness-reference-contrast-source-20261018/revision02-B0-schedule/ordinary-QA/build/witness-reference-contrast-positive\",\n        \"--exact\",\n        \"factorial_two_complete_prefix_program_cache_and_incomplete_stream\",\n        \"--test-threads=1\",\n        \"--nocapture\"\n      ],\n      \"cwd\": \"/home/charl/Moriarty/.moriarty-dev/runtime/sherlock-review-20261017/witness-reference-contrast-source-20261018/revision02-B0-schedule/ordinary-QA\",\n      \"environment\": {\n        \"PATH\": \"/usr/bin:/bin\",\n        \"LANG\": \"C.UTF-8\",\n        \"TMPDIR\": \"/home/charl/Moriarty/.moriarty-dev/runtime/sherlock-review-20261017/witness-reference-contrast-source-20261018/revision02-B0-schedule/ordinary-QA/tmp\"\n      },\n      \"expected_selected_tests\": 1,\n      \"expected_status\": \"ONE_SELECTED_TEST_PASS_ONLY_IF_AC