 \"cae5d50f33ceda8f9039bd4bcc34594cdcb56b7acaab97c021ce767be99ebc2a\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"actualCoreReceipt\": {\n    \"path\": \"/home/charl/Moriarty/.moriarty-dev/runtime/sherlock-review-20261017/witness-reference-projection-ordinary-QA-20261018/actual-five-01/RESULT.json\",\n    \"bytes\": 66419,\n    \"sha256\": \"0d974b2b53517b15678cc1498f4ff74736fa319c457829e8404aa7052adc4980\"\n  },\n  \"bounds\": \"Compile30s CPU25 AS2GiB FSIZE64MiB CORE0; eachnewexacttest10s CPU8 AS1GiB FSIZE16MiB CORE0;131072 bytes each stream; serial fail-stop one attempt no retry.\",\n  \"capture\": \"Existing R435 revision02 capture(op,newphase) callback only. No old main, old selection/ledger or new runner.\",\n  \"membership\": \"Each literal exact test must report running1/pass1/fail0/ignored0/measured0/filtered1; zero tests fail; no output digest invented before actual success.\",\n  \"newB0Predicate\": \"Factorial2 only: compare complete independently frozen clockPrefixColumns/clockPrefixes/intervals with actual raw B counters/rules/event-to-semantic-boundary associations; no A=B clocks.\",\n  \"otherThreeB0SchedulesSelected\": false,\n  \"authorExposure\": {\n    \"path\": \"/home/charl/Moriarty/.moriarty-dev/runtime/sherlock-review-20261017/witness-reference-contrast-source-20261018/revision02-B0-schedule/AUTHOR-EXPOSURE-PROVENANCE.json\",\n    \"bytes\": 820,\n    \"sha256\": \"a74a1f7f14fd157ec25e29ccda1d061658b616b6f9d767e83c7b6b5ce23188f4\"\n  },\n  \"opaqueBodiesReadByAuthor\": false,\n  \"whole035Closure\": false,\n  \"notSelected\": [\n    \"normalCore recompile\",\n    \"Core cfg(test)\",\n    \"old passing three projector tests\",\n    \"old cache tests\",\n    \"Cargo/buildscripts\",\n    \"SDK/native/models/provider\",\n    \"hostile malformed WitnessPlan/guard tests\"\n  ]\n}\n\n=== END FULL BODY 09-exact-three-operations ===\n\n=== BEGIN FULL BODY 10-scope-and-exposure | /home/charl/Moriarty/.moriarty-dev/runtime/sherlock-review-20261017/witness-reference-contrast-source-20261018/revision02-B0-schedule/INTERFACES-AND-SCOPE.md | 2774 bytes | SHA256 28f3f330ef66e3df97cb25d3a200f98be66351a34eaa8cd4d4550351adc96839 ===\n# Additive B0 schedule comparison\n\nThis revision preserves the original two-case consumer cut and adds one comparison call plus appended diagnostic functions. No product library, witness strategy, guard, source program, A oracle, source-association probe or stream-resume assertion changes. Only the new factorial2 run invokes the B0 comparison; the other original three independently expected B0 schedules are retained for future predicates and are not selected or replayed here.\n\nThe consumer walks every complete saved raw B record in the actual translated spans. It reads consumed work, helper work, helper visits, reference cursor and remaining work directly from each actual image and checks changes against actual event deltas. It retains a genesis row and one row after every actual B record, including helpers, charged bookkeeping and free publication. It never derives B costs from A charges. Source-event positions and interval joins come from actual spans; the semantic snapshot index stutters across helper rows and advances at the separate actual completion/publication. Those association arrays are checked against the full independent contract, not accepted from an expected array. The complete public RuleIdC-to-dotted-name mapping is declaration data from the independent safe schema; it reveals no selected schedule.\n\nAll actual arrays are constructed before the runtime opaque fixture is parsed. The complete `clockPrefixColumns`, `clockPrefixes` and `intervals` arrays are compared structurally, along with actual run profile/domain/initial fuel. The original complete A39 prefix comparisons remain unchanged. Raw physical B images and helper phases stay available in spans; this is finite counter/schedule/semantic-boundary association testing, not a proof of raw-image refinement or global correspondence.\n\nRoot disclo